\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  action will help lead to the drug being available through online orders and delivery by mail. PHOTO: Ilana Panich-Linsman for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration on Thursday relaxed restrictions around an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/SB970157748237129306"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  pill }}}\uc2  that had prevented women from getting the medication without first making in-person visits to pick up the prescriptions at medical offices.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  decision to allow patients to get the drug mifepristone, sold under the brand name Mifeprex and sometimes known as RU-486, without a visit to a hospital or doctor will help pave the way for the drug to be available for ordering online and delivery by mail, according to groups that support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  said in a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.fda.gov/drugs/postmarket-drug-safety-information-patients-and-providers/questions-and-answers-mifeprex"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 document posted on its website }}}\uc2  that it was ending a requirement restricting where mifepristone could be dispensed to certain healthcare settings, such as clinics, medical offices and hospitals.\par \par \uc2 The agency said it also was adding a requirement that pharmacies that dispense the medication be certified.\par \par \uc2 Organizations that support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights applauded the action, which follows a lawsuit brought by \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  challenging the in-person requirement.\par \par \uc2 "This decision follows the science, something we could only hope for from our nation's regulatory body on medications," said Dr. Jamila Perritt, president and chief executive of Physicians for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Health\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "And the science shows that medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care is safe to administer via telehealth."\par \par \uc2 Other groups, including organizations that oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said the \uc2 FDA\uc2  decision ignored data that mifepristone leads to more emergency room visits.\par \par \uc2 "Today's \uc2 FDA\uc2  decision ignores several sets of much more substantial data which confirms the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pill is a significant public health threat, and the real-world data suggests that threat is growing," said Dr. James Studnicki, vice president of data analytics at Charlotte Lozier Institute, a group that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 New York Times\uc2  earlier reported the \uc2 FDA\uc2  action.\par \par \uc2 Mifepristone, used up to the first 10 weeks of pregnancy, works by halting the supply of hormones that maintain the interior of the uterus, according to the Mayo Clinic.\par \par \uc2 During the Trump administration, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  responded to the pandemic by relaxing certain requirements for drugs, and encouraged telemedicine, to help prevent transmission. However, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  didn't relax the restrictions requiring in-person pick up for the drug mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 , an organization of women's healthcare physicians, and other groups sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  over its exclusion of mifepristone.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-restores-mandate-that-women-pick-up-abortion-drugs-in-person-11610500527"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court in January, however, agreed with the Trump administration }}}\uc2  on excluding the drug.\par \par \uc2 In May, the \uc2 FDA\uc2  said it would review the restrictions around the medication, which is used in abortions and miscarriages.\par \par \uc2 Write to Stephanie Armour at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:stephanie.armour@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stephanie.armour@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/fda-allows-women-to-get-abortion-pill-by-mail-11639698022"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 FDA Allows Women to Get \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Pill by Mail  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020211216ehcg00899\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
