\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Arizona Asks Supreme Court to Reinstate  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law; State requests emergency order to reverse lower court's block on legislation criminalizing abortions for fetal abnormalities\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jess Bravin \par \uc2 735 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 December 2021\par 20:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The state of Arizona asked the Supreme Court Tuesday for an emergency order reinstating a law passed earlier this year that imposes criminal penalties for abortions performed because of fetal genetic abnormalities.\par \par \uc2 Lower courts, noting the law likely violated Supreme Court precedents entitling women to end unwanted pregnancies, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/judge-temporarily-blocks-parts-of-new-arizona-abortion-law-11632936417"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have blocked enforcement of the measure  }}}\uc2  while a challenge filed by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and allied nonprofit organizations proceeds.\par \par \uc2 "This Court has never otherwise recognized the purported right at issue\u8212\'20\'14a right to race-, sex-, or genetic-selective abortions," the state's brief says, although only the genetic-abnormality provision is at issue in the case.\par \par \uc2 Arizona's application is the latest in a series of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases reaching the Supreme Court, where a recently expanded conservative majority has expressed deep skepticism of Roe v. Wade, the 1973 decision recognizing women's right to end unwanted pregnancies before fetal viability.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Tuesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in Texas asked the court to expedite issuance of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rules-abortion-clinics-can-challenge-texas-abortion-law-11639149404"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 its Friday ruling  }}}\uc2  that permitted their suit challenging that state's ban on ending pregnancies after six weeks' gestation to proceed against officials of the state medical board and other licensing agencies. The Texas law remains in effect and the providers hope that expediting the proceedings could help them more rapidly obtain at least a partial victory at the trial court. The state of Texas opposes the providers' application.\par \par \uc2 In another case, heard Dec. 1, Mississippi {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-in-landmark-mississippi-abortion-case-11638354602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked the court to overrule Roe altogether  }}}\uc2  in arguing to reinstate its ban on abortions after 15 weeks, which lower courts found in violation of Roe and a 1992 case that narrowed but didn't extinguish it holding, \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  v. Casey.\par \par \uc2 In 2011, Arizona outlawed abortions performed because of the race or sex of the fetus. This year, the state legislature added genetic abnormalities to that ban, finding "that in the United States and abroad fetuses with Down syndrome are disproportionately targeted for abortions." The act sends, the legislation says, "an unambiguous message that children with genetic abnormalities, whether born or unborn, are equal in dignity and value to their peers without genetic abnormalities, born or unborn."\par \par \uc2 The statute also indicates that should Roe be overruled, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  immediately will be outlawed in Arizona. The measure declares that "an unborn child at every stage of development, [holds] all rights, privileges and immunities available to other persons, citizens and residents of this state," limited only by the Constitution and its interpretation by the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 With some narrow exceptions, the Arizona law imposes penalties, fines, imprisonment and civil liability for performing or financing prohibited abortions; women who undergo the procedure face no punishment.\par \par \uc2 Two physicians, along with the Arizona Medical Association and state sections of the National Council of Jewish Women and the \uc2 National Organization for Women\uc2  , sued to invalidate the 2021 measure. In September, a federal judge in Phoenix blocked enforcement of much of the law while that suit proceeded.\par \par \uc2 "Arizona law does not offer workable guidance about which fetal conditions bring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care within the scope of these provisions," U.S. District Judge Douglas Rayes found. Moreover, he wrote, physicians may not be sure of a patient's true motivation in obtaining the procedure.\par \par \uc2 "At what point can a doctor be deemed to 'know' or 'believe' what is in the mind of a patient?" he wrote. "This problem is exacerbated by the reality that the decision to terminate a pregnancy is a complex one, and often is motivated by a variety of considerations, some of which are inextricably intertwined with the detection of a fetal genetic abnormality."\par \par \uc2 Last month, the Ninth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals, in San Francisco, without comment declined to reinstate the law during the litigation, prompting Arizona's application to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 Arizona's application was filed with Justice \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  , who oversees the Ninth Circuit. She is likely to request a response from the plaintiffs before deciding whether to act on her own or refer the matter to the full court. There is no deadline for the Supreme Court to act, but emergency applications often are decided within days or weeks.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jess.bravin+1@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jess.bravin+1@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arizona-asks-supreme-court-to-reinstate-abortion-law-11639514794"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arizona Asks Supreme Court to Reinstate \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020211214ehce00565\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
