\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 California's \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  Favors Gun Suits Modeled on Texas  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law; Governor's proposal would allow private citizens to sue manufacturers in the state for at least $10,000 per violation\b0\par\par\uc2 By Christine Mai-Duc \par \uc2 532 \uc2 words\par \uc2 12 December 2021\par 20:18 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 California Gov. \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2  said he wants to create a path for private citizens to sue gun manufacturers, sellers and distributors in the state, modeling his proposal after the legal framework used in the Texas law that bans abortions past six weeks.\par \par \uc2 On the heels of Friday's \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  ruling allowing the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rules-abortion-clinics-can-challenge-texas-abortion-law-11639149404"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas law to remain in effect  }}}\uc2  for now, Mr. Newsom said he would work with the Democratic-dominated Legislature and Attorney General \uc2 Rob Bonta\uc2  , also a Democrat, to draft a proposal.\par \par \uc2 The bill would allow private citizens to sue anyone who manufactures, sells or distributes assault weapons or ghost gun kits or parts in the state for at least $10,000 per violation.\par \par \uc2 The state of Texas had used a similar mechanism in an attempt to insulate its \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban from legal review, assigning enforcement authority to private civil litigants instead of public officials. The \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  on Friday did give \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers a narrow legal path to challenge the Texas ban.\par \par \uc2 In June, a federal judge {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/judge-overturns-california-ban-on-assault-weapons-11622900535"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down California's 32-year-old ban  }}}\uc2  on certain weapons, likening AR-15 rifles to Swiss Army knives. The ruling {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/appeals-court-upholds-californias-ban-on-some-firearm-magazines-11638303445"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 was subsequently put on hold  }}}\uc2  pending appeal. Last month a federal appeals court upheld the state's ban on high-capacity magazines.\par \par \uc2 "If states can now shield their laws from review by the federal courts that compare assault weapons to Swiss Army knives, then California will use that authority to protect people's lives, where Texas used it to put women in harm's way," Mr. Newsom said in a statement Saturday.\par \par \uc2 At last month's \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  arguments over the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  asked the state's lawyer about concerns raised in a brief from the Firearms Policy Coalition predicting proposals like Mr. Newsom's.\par \par \uc2 "This will easily become the model for suppression of other constitutional rights, with Second Amendment rights being the most likely targets," Justice Kavanaugh said.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  and the court's three liberal justices warned in dissent to Friday's ruling that the limited ruling could inflict long-term damage on the protection of constitutional rights. "Texas has employed an array of stratagems designed to shield its unconstitutional law from judicial review," the chief justice wrote.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Newsom's office, which laid out the proposal Saturday evening, didn't provide additional details including timing for a bill or whether legislative leaders or Mr. Bonta had signed on in support. Mr. Bonta, Assembly Speaker Anthony Rendon and Senate leader \uc2 Toni Atkins\uc2  didn't respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 As the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  weighs protections for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Mr. Newsom and other state leaders have said they want to make California a sanctuary for women from out of state who are seeking to end their pregnancies, which {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/california-may-pay-expenses-for-women-seeking-abortions-from-other-states-11638996688"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 could include paying for abortions  }}}\uc2  and other related costs.\par \par \uc2 Write to Christine Mai-Duc at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:christine.maiduc@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 christine.maiduc@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/californias-gavin-newsom-proposes-letting-citizens-sue-gun-makers-11639281730"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 California's Gavin Newsom Favors Gun Suits Modeled on Texas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020211212ehcc00001\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
