\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Illinois  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Clinics Are Preparing for a Potential Post-Roe World;  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  providers say they are already seeing influx of patients from out of state\u8211\'20\'13and expect more\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jennifer Calfas \par \uc2 1,381 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 December 2021\par 10:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 As the Supreme Court weighs a case that could chip away at federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections under Roe v. Wade, providers in Illinois are preparing for a potential surge of patients.\par \par \uc2 The case before the high court, Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization, centers on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com/articles/mississippi-asks-supreme-court-to-end-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-11626985810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions enacted }}}\uc2  hundreds of miles away in Mississippi. But in its brief, Mississippi took direct aim at the 1973 Roe decision, arguing the ruling tramples states' rights. The justices {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-in-landmark-mississippi-abortion-case-11638354602"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heard oral arguments }}}\uc2  Wednesday, and several conservative justices signaled they might be receptive to the state's arguments. A decision is expected no later than next summer.\par \par \uc2 Should the high court weaken Roe, state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws would become all the more significant. Striking it down altogether would mean \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws revert to states.\par \par \uc2 Illinois, where Democrats control the governor's office and Legislature, enshrined the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in state law in 2019. It is one of more than a dozen states to have passed laws protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, including New York and California. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
