\par \par \uc2 A medical assistant sterilizes an ultrasound transducer, or probe, at Hope Clinic for Women, an independent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  provider in Granite City, Ill. PHOTO: Whitney Curtis for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Conversely, 12 states have passed trigger laws that would automatically or quickly outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should Roe be overturned.\par \par \uc2 Defenders and opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights say Illinois would be both a haven for those seeking the procedure and a threat to those working to restrict access in bordering states. Several other states where courts or lawmakers have protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, including Nevada, Minnesota and Kansas, also share borders with states that have more stringent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws.\par \par \uc2 Illinois borders five states that could ban or further restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if federal protections are weakened or overturned, according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2 , a research group that supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Wisconsin, whose Democratic governor and Republican-controlled state Legislature often spar over policy, is one of eight states with unenforced \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans\u8212\'20\'14made before Roe\u8212\'20\'14still on the books.\par \par \uc2 Missouri and Kentucky have trigger laws in place. Iowa passed a law banning abortions after six weeks of pregnancy that isn't in effect. The \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  said it anticipates Indiana could take steps to outlaw the procedure based on other legislative efforts there over the past decade. \par \par {\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw640\pich426\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal9600\pichgoal6390
