\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court to Review Mississippi's 15-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; State wants Roe v. Wade overruled and women's right to end unwanted pregnancies abolished\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jess Bravin and Brent Kendall \par \uc2 1,043 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 November 2021\par 13:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14Mississippi will ask the Supreme Court at Wednesday arguments to overrule Roe v. Wade and eliminate the constitutional right women have held since 1973 to end unwanted pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 The case provides the first direct test of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-says-abortion-rights-could-be-decided-by-states-1530474523"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 2016 campaign prediction }}}\uc2  that if he got the opportunity to make two or three appointments to the Supreme Court, Roe "automatically" would be overruled. Three Trump appointees\u8212\'20\'14two of whom succeeded justices who voted to affirm \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights\u8212\'20\'14now sit on the court.\par \par \uc2 Separately, a decision is pending on a Texas law passed in May that bans \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after about six weeks. The court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-hears-arguments-on-texas-abortion-law-11635765801"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 heard arguments }}}\uc2  on Nov. 1 after having voted 5-4 in September to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allow the law to take effect }}}\uc2 . The majority cited the law's provision that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-in-court-what-you-need-to-know-11631730720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 private parties rather than state officials }}}\uc2  enforce the law through civil litigation, a procedural device Texas lawmakers included to stymie judicial review.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Is there a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The court may find a way through the Mississippi case without overruling Roe. Apart from any affirmation of lower courts that found the measure unconstitutional, it could uphold the Mississippi law by further restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights without abolishing them altogether.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi law }}}\uc2 , which was immediately blocked by a federal judge, forbids women more than 15 weeks pregnant from obtaining abortions. The state's only provider, the Jackson Women's Health Organization, sued to strike down the ban. The clinic doesn't perform the procedure after 16 weeks and, according to court records, the law would halt about 100 of more than 2,000 abortions performed annually in Mississippi.\par \par \uc2 A report this month from the \uc2 Centers for Disease Control and Prevention\uc2  estimated that roughly 95% of abortions take place by 15 weeks of gestation. Nearly 44% are now performed through the administration of medications in the early weeks of pregnancy instead of surgery, the CDC report found.\par \par \uc2 The Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals, in New Orleans, affirmed a district judge who found the Mississippi Gestational Age Act unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 "In an unbroken line dating to Roe v. Wade, the Supreme Court's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases have established (and affirmed, and re-affirmed) a woman's right to choose an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before viability," Judge Patrick Higginbotham wrote for the Fifth Circuit. "States may regulate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  procedures prior to viability so long as they do not impose an undue burden on the woman's right, but they may not ban abortions."\par \par \uc2 Fetal viability, or the ability to live outside the womb, arises at about 24 weeks. The majority in the 1992 case Planned Parenthood v. Casey, in an effort to find middle ground, pared back but didn't eliminate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and laid out the undue-burden standard. Because the Gestational Age Act would outlaw only a fraction of the Jackson clinic's caseload, the state argued it couldn't be considered an undue burden.\par \par \uc2 Mississippi's law was initially designed as a more incremental attack on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a different epoch of Supreme Court history. When the state Gestational Age Act was adopted in March 2018, Justices \uc2 Anthony Kennedy\uc2  and \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  sat on the court, where legal views all but foreclosed the chance of finding five justices ready to significantly limit \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Justice Kennedy had retired but Justice Ginsburg remained active in June 2020, when Mississippi appealed the Fifth Circuit's ruling. In its initial brief, the state argued that the Supreme Court wouldn't have to overrule Roe to decide in its favor, but simply to reconcile what it argued were conflicting strands of precedent regarding viability as the constitutional limit for banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The legal calculation changed when Justice Ginsburg died in September 2020, affording Mr. Trump the opportunity to fill the vacancy with Justice Amy Coney Barrett.\par \par \uc2 Then-Judge Barrett didn't declare her position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights during confirmation hearings in October 2020, but Senate Judiciary Committee Chairman \uc2 Lindsey Graham\uc2  (R., S.C.) called it "the first time in American history that we've nominated a woman who's unashamedly pro-life and embraces her faith without apology."\par \par \uc2 Democrats didn't disagree. "Judge Barrett has a long record of opposing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Vice President Kamala Harris, then a member of the \uc2 Senate Judiciary Committee\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After the court agreed in May to hear Mississippi's appeal, the state brought on a new lawyer, former Trump Justice Department official Scott Stewart, who raised a bold new claim: "Roe and Casey are egregiously wrong," he said, and should be overruled.\par \par \uc2 In addition to asserting that the court erred in recognizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in 1973, Mississippi also argues that rationales for maintaining Roe, including the autonomy women gain through greater control of their reproductive lives, have lost urgency.\par \par \uc2 "Today, adoption is accessible and on a wide scale women attain both professional success and a rich family life, contraceptives are more available and effective, and scientific advances show that an unborn child has taken on the human form and features months before viability," Mississippi's brief says.\par \par \uc2 The Jackson clinic, in its response brief, says Mississippi is recycling arguments that courts have long rejected, including in the 1992 Casey decision.\par \par \uc2 "Unless the Court is to be perceived as representing nothing more than the preferences of its current membership, it is critical that judicial protection hold firm absent the most dramatic and unexpected changes in law or fact," says the clinic, which is represented by the \uc2 Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 If the court does overturn Roe, however, Mississippi's 15-week ban effectively will become irrelevant. The state is one of at least 21 with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans that predate 1973 or statutes that immediately will outlaw the procedure should the Supreme Court conclude the Constitution provides women no right to end unwanted pregnancies.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jess.bravin+1@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jess.bravin+1@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Brent Kendall at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:brent.kendall@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brent.kendall@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-review-mississippis-15-week-abortion-ban-11638278936"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court to Review Mississippi's 15-Week \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020211130ehbu002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
