\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Biden Leads Democratic Push to Block New  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Restrictions After Shifting Stance in Campaign; President described his position on  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  as 'middle of the road' in past, backed Hyde curbs until 2019\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 1,374 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 November 2021\par 10:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 As the Supreme Court prepares to consider a big test to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, President Biden is leading Democratic efforts to block new restrictions on the procedure, following a campaign shift toward the views of a liberal Democratic Party.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-mississippi-abortion-case-supreme-court-sets-arguments-for-december-11632176939"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The court will hear arguments on Dec. 1  }}}\uc2  over a Mississippi law that seeks to ban most abortions after 15 weeks, giving the justices an opening to revisit the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision and later rulings that upheld a woman's constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-administration-prepares-to-sue-texas-over-abortion-law-11631151641"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. Biden's administration is challenging a Texas law  }}}\uc2  that effectively bans abortions after six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden, a practicing Catholic, described his position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as "middle of the road" in the past. But he has sought to stay in step with a Democratic Party that has rejected policies that would limit access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and turned away from candidates with reservations on the issue. That has presented challenges, such as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bishops-vote-to-prepare-document-on-communion-for-catholic-politicians-who-support-abortion-rights-11624041010?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 criticism from U.S. Catholic bishops  }}}\uc2 , and risks limiting his appeal to some voters.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How could President Biden's personal beliefs on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights affect the action his administration takes? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 "It feels like his position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and a lot of issues has morphed with the Democratic Party," said Dan Green, national communications director of Democrats for Life, an advocacy group for antiabortion Democrats. "A lot of pro-life Democrats were hopeful that he would at least listen to our concerns and have some sort of inclusive language in the party platform."\par \par \uc2 A White House official said Mr. Biden has long made clear that he will "not impose his personal faith on others," adding that "he will continue to stand side-by-side with women across the country to protect their constitutional rights." The official also said Mr. Biden believes there is space in the Democratic Party for those who oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, citing {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-meet-with-pope-francis-ahead-of-g-20-summit-11634222170"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his nomination of former Sen. Joe Donnelly  }}}\uc2 , an antiabortion Democrat, to serve as U.S. ambassador to the Vatican.\par \par \uc2 In his 2007 memoir, Mr. Biden described what he called his "middle of the road" position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which included opposing federal funding for the procedure and voting against late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . During his Democratic primary campaign in 2019, he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-reverses-stance-on-hyde-amendment-citing-roe-v-wade-11559871101"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversed his long-held support  }}}\uc2  for the Hyde Amendment, which bans federal funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , except for victims of rape and incest.\par \par \uc2 "I continue to be a strong supporter of Roe v. Wade," Mr. Biden said from the White House in September, reacting to the Texas law. But reflecting his longstanding view that many people have conflicting feelings on the issue, he quickly followed: "I respect people who don't support Roe v. Wade; I respect their views."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's efforts have prompted criticism from U.S. Catholic bishops, a challenge for the nation's second Catholic president, a regular mass-goer who often speaks openly about his faith.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this year, some sought to adopt a national policy that would deny Communion to politicians who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, such as Mr. Biden, but the Vatican warned that such a policy could be divisive. Asked about the controversy in September, \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  said that bishops shouldn't politicize the reception of Communion. At their fall meeting, the bishops {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/catholic-bishops-drop-effort-to-ban-communion-for-politicians-who-support-abortion-rights-11637169752?mod=djemalertNEWS"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 passed new guidance on Communion  }}}\uc2  that doesn't address the issue.\par \par \uc2 Following a meeting at the Vatican in October, Mr. Biden told reporters that the pope told him to continue receiving Communion, and that the pope told him he was a "good Catholic." The Vatican hasn't commented on Mr. Biden's description of the exchange.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's shift leftward on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  reflects a move in both parties away from the center, with national Democratic politicians now nearly uniformly embracing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and Republican politicians overwhelmingly antiabortion. When Mr. Biden came to Washington in 1973, there were more Democrats who supported limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and more Republicans who backed some access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The transition started decades ago in both parties, historians said. Mary Ziegler, a legal historian at \uc2 Florida State University\uc2  who studies \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , noted that President \uc2 Ronald Reagan\uc2  , a Republican, embraced the antiabortion position in an effort to appeal to conservative Catholics and evangelical voters. Members of the Democratic Party who opposed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access faced primary challenges funded by groups like Emily's List, and Republicans faced similar litmus tests to oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 "Both the Republican Party and the Democratic Party have abandoned the idea of catering to the median voter," Ms. Ziegler said.\par \par \uc2 While the political parties have grown increasingly entrenched on the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  issue, Americans continue to have mixed views, including Catholics.\par \par \uc2 Polls show {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://news.gallup.com/poll/1576/abortion.aspx"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most Americans say \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  should be legal  }}}\uc2  under some or all circumstances. The \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2  has found that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.pewresearch.org/fact-tank/2020/10/20/8-key-findings-about-catholics-and-abortion/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 56% of U.S. Catholics believe \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  should be legal  }}}\uc2  in all or most cases, and 68% believe Roe v. Wade shouldn't be overturned.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden has spoken publicly about \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the years, saying it has been hard to take positions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that put him at odds with the U.S. bishops. But he has also said he sought to avoid imposing his religious beliefs on others.\par \par \uc2 "I'm prepared to accept that at the moment of conception there's human life and being, but I'm not prepared to say that to other God-fearing, non-God-fearing people that have a different view," Mr. Biden said in a 2015 interview with America Magazine, which is published by the Jesuit order of the Catholic Church.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's 2019 shift on the Hyde Amendment funding ban came after pressure from \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates and Democratic opponents. People familiar with his decision said Mr. Biden was persuaded by the argument that if he included the Hyde Amendment in his healthcare plan, it would be discriminatory against poor and minority women who are Medicaid recipients, because the program doesn't pay for abortions with federal funds except in limited circumstances.\par \par \uc2 In a speech in Atlanta following the reversal, Mr. Biden said: "It was not under attack\u8230\'20\'26as it is now. But circumstances have changed."\par \par \uc2 Since taking office, Mr. Biden {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-budget-plan-would-remove-ban-on-federal-funds-for-abortion-11622231319"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped the Hyde Amendment from his budget proposal  }}}\uc2 . His administration has asked the Supreme Court to block the Texas law, which prohibits abortions after "cardiac activity" can be detected. For most pregnancies, that happens at around two weeks after a woman has missed her period. The Supreme Court recently heard arguments over whether the federal government and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers can challenge it.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden also has drawn complaints from advocates that he hasn't been a vocal enough proponent of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access, including that he didn't use the word \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a statement marking the anniversary of Roe v. Wade, which advocates see as important to show support for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 A bill that would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions before fetal viability passed the House in September with just one Democrat, Rep. \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  of Texas, voting against it. Among Republicans, House members are united in their opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and in the Senate just Sens. \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  (R., Maine) and \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2  (R., Alaska) support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 The partisan divide on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  highlights how much has changed since Mr. Biden came to Washington in 1973, when there were more centrist politicians on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in both parties. Some former elected officials said that the polarization on the issue made it harder for Democrats and Republicans to work together.\par \par \uc2 "When issues don't cut across party lines, that means that's one fewer issue where some Democrats and Republicans can see eye to eye on," said former Rep. \uc2 Dan Lipinski\uc2  (D., Ill.), an antiabortion Catholic who was defeated in a Democratic primary in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Said former Rep. Charlie Dent, a Pennsylvania Republican who supported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights: "You lose the ability to find consensus."\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-abortion-restrictions-supreme-court-mississippi-texas-11638024836"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden Leads Democratic Push to Block New \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Restrictions After Shifting Stance in Campaign  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020211128ehbs00002\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
