\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Catholic Bishops Drop Effort to Ban Communion for Politicians Who Support  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights; The vote was the culmination of a debate that has exposed deep ideological divisions between U.S. bishops and the Vatican\b0\par\par\uc2 By Ian Lovett and Francis X. Rocca \par \uc2 962 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 November 2021\par 22:14 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 BALTIMORE\u8212\'20\'14The Catholic bishops of the U.S. ended a nearly yearlong debate Wednesday over whether to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bishops-vote-to-prepare-document-on-communion-for-catholic-politicians-who-support-abortion-rights-11624041010"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 bar politicians who support \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2 from receiving the Eucharist, passing new guidance on Communion that doesn't address the issue.\par \par \uc2 The measure passed by a vote of 222-8 and was followed by applause at a gathering here of the U.S. Conference of Catholic Bishops.\par \par \uc2 The vote was the culmination of a debate that has taken most of the year and exposed deep ideological divisions in the church\u8212\'20\'14particularly between U.S. bishops and Rome.\par \par \uc2 Conservatives in the U.S. had pushed to issue guidelines that would clearly advise clergy not to offer Communion to politicians who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, a category that includes President Biden.\par \par \uc2 But the Vatican warned that such a policy could be divisive, and \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  said the bishops shouldn't politicize the reception of Communion. Last month, after the two men met at the Vatican, Mr. Biden told reporters that \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  had called him a good Catholic and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.google.com/search?q=wsj biden pope&rlz=1C1GCEB_enUS827US827&oq=wsj biden pope&aqs=chrome..69i57j69i60l2.2119j0j7&sourceid=chrome&ie=UTF-8"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 told him to continue receiving Communion }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Regardless of any guidance from the USCCB, individual bishops ultimately have the power under church law to deny Communion. Cardinal \uc2 Wilton Gregory\uc2 , who as archbishop of Washington, D.C., is the president's pastor, has said that he wouldn't refuse him Communion.\par \par \uc2 Archbishop Salvatore Cordileone of San Francisco, who has said that the president shouldn't take Communion, has criticized House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2 , a Catholic whose home district is in his archdiocese, for her support of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. In an interview Wednesday, he said he didn't expect Mrs. Pelosi would present herself for Communion in San Francisco, but wouldn't offer it to her if she did.\par \par \uc2 At a June conference, bishops voted 168 to 55, with six abstentions, to prepare a document on the Eucharist that would address the conditions under which Catholics can receive Communion, including potentially how that would be affected by politicians' position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Ultimately, the bishops acquiesced to the pontiff, approving a document that celebrates the Eucharist and offers general guidance on its reception but doesn't mention \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  or elected officials in regard to eligibility for the sacrament.\par \par \uc2 During debate on the floor Wednesday, one bishop after another spoke in favor of the document\u8212\'20\'14a stark departure from their June meeting, when conservatives and liberals fought over what sort of guidance was appropriate. The bishops met repeatedly in private sessions this week, an unusual step that allowed them to reach an agreement out of the public eye.\par \par \uc2 "This has been a complex work," Joseph Naumann, archbishop of Kansas City and head of the USCCB's pro-life committee, said during the public session on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 He voted in favor of Wednesday's guidance. In an interview, Archbishop Naumann said it included "pretty much what I was hoping for." Noting that it is up to individual bishops to make decisions about offering Communion, he added, "What we can do is say something to encourage and empower bishops to have these difficult conversations with legislators." When prominent Catholics don't follow church teaching, he said, it can lead people into error.\par \par \uc2 Bishop John Stowe, of Lexington, Ky., who earlier this year tried to stop efforts to issue any document with new guidance related to the Eucharist, said he was grateful the final product "doesn't name politicians and doesn't get into a whole list of who may and who may not" receive Communion.\par \par \uc2 "You have to follow \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 ' line," he said. If the president or Mrs. Pelosi sought to receive Communion in his diocese, he said, he would offer it.\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  has often reaffirmed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pope-francis-faces-tests-on-abortion-gay-rights-11632913201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the church's condemnation of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2 , but has taken a friendly approach to the president.\par \par \uc2 His envoy to the U.S., Archbishop Christophe Pierre, said Tuesday that polarization in society was echoing through the church and called for a more conciliatory approach.\par \par \uc2 "There is a temptation to treat the Eucharist as something to be offered to the privileged few," Archbishop Pierre said, "rather than to seek to walk with those whose theology or discipleship is falling short."\par \par \uc2 Though the church must be "unapologetically pro-life," the archbishop said, it was important to understand and address the social problems that lead women to seek abortions.\par \par \uc2 A document advising against giving the sacrament to politicians who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights would have been a public rebuke for Mr. Biden, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-trump-catholic-voters-presidential-election-abortion-supreme-court-11600961731"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who has made his faith }}}\uc2  a major part of his public persona. A \uc2 Pew Research Center\uc2  study this year found 55% of Catholics believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in most or all cases, compared with 59% of Americans overall. A Pew report released last year said 67% of Catholics who attend Mass weekly believe \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be illegal in most or all cases.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tensions\par \par \uc2 More WSJ coverage of the issue, in religion and politics, selected by the editors\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-pope-francis-meet-amid-controversy-over-abortion-11635502337"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden Says Pope Told Him He Is a Good Catholic Amid Controversy Over \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  (Oct. 29)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pope-francis-and-president-biden-to-meet-as-both-face-abortion-tensions-with-u-s-bishops-11635327000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pope Francis and President Biden to Meet as Both Face \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Tensions With U.S. Bishops }}}\uc2  (Oct. 27)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-agrees-to-quick-consideration-of-texas-abortion-case-leaves-state-law-in-place-for-now-11634921299"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court Agrees to Quick Consideration of Texas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law }}}\uc2  (Oct. 22)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pope-francis-faces-tests-on-abortion-gay-rights-11632913201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pope Francis Faces Tests on \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 , Gay Rights }}}\uc2  (Sept. 29)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bishops-vote-to-prepare-document-on-communion-for-catholic-politicians-who-support-abortion-rights-11624041010"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bishops Advance Effort That Could Restrict Communion for Biden }}}\uc2  (June 18)\par \par \uc2 Write to Ian Lovett at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:ian.lovett@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ian.lovett@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Francis X. Rocca at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:francis.rocca@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 francis.rocca@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/catholic-bishops-drop-effort-to-ban-communion-for-politicians-who-support-abortion-rights-11637169752"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Catholic Bishops Drop Effort to Ban Communion for Politicians Who Support \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rights }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020211117ehbh004jx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
