\par \par \uc2 Valerie Register (in a photo from last month) said she had voted for Republican Glenn Youngkin on Tuesday in part because she shared his antiabortion views. PHOTO: Carlos Bernate for The Wall Street Journal\par \par \uc2 Mandeep Kaur, 25, who works in human resources, said she voted for Mr. McAuliffe because she believed he would protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and support immigration, among other issues.\par \par \uc2 "We saw what happened in Texas with \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Ms. Kaur, who said she became a citizen last year after immigrating from India. "I think women should have the choice."\par \par \uc2 Charles Armstead, 73, said he voted for Mr. McAuliffe. "I think that the Republicans are still too entrapped by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and his ideals," said Mr. Armstead, who said he is an independent voter and a Defense Department consultant and retired Air Force officer. He said he worried that Republicans would restrict voting rights.\par \par \uc2 In Virginia Beach, Valerie Register said she voted Tuesday morning for Mr. Youngkin on her way back from the gym. The 53-year-old software developer said she shared his antiabortion views. She also said she thought he would roll back what she sees as growing government interference in areas such as gun ownership and Covid-19 vaccination decisions.\par \par \uc2 "It seems like we're headed down the wrong road where they're trying to push into more and more government control. By voting for Youngkin, I believe we're trying to pull back on that," she said.\par \par \uc2 Voters in New Jersey also voted for a governor Tuesday. Late Tuesday night, Democratic \uc2 Gov. Phil Murphy\uc2  was narrowly behind Republican Jack Ciattarelli, a former state assemblyman. The candidates have clashed over fiscal issues as well as Mr. Murphy's requirement for students to wear masks in schools. Three nonpartisan surveys released in the past week showed Mr. Murphy leading by roughly 10 points over Mr. Ciattarelli.\par \par \uc2 Virginia Democrats are also vying to retain control of the state's house of delegates. In 2019, Democrats gained majorities in both the House and state Senate, giving them a trifecta, with Mr. Northam already in the governor's office. Democrats hold a 55-45 advantage in the House, and all 100 seats are up for election. None of the 40 Senate seats are on the ballot.\par \par \uc2 Across the U.S., there are 23 Republican trifectas, 15 Democratic trifectas, and 12 divided governments where neither party holds trifecta control, according to election-data website Ballotpedia.\par \par \uc2 As Election Day neared, Republican voters in Virginia appeared more excited than Democrats, according to a poll released last week by Christopher Newport University's Wason Center for Civic Leadership. It found 80% of Republican likely voters said they were very enthusiastic, compared with 65% of Democrats. That "enthusiasm advantage" has grown since its Oct. 8 survey, the center said.\par \par \uc2 The poll found that independent voters favor Mr. Youngkin over Mr. McAuliffe 51% to 44%. For Mr. Youngkin, key sources of support are white voters, men and residents of Virginia's southern and southwestern areas, the poll found, whereas Mr. McAuliffe's support is strongest among Black voters, women and Northern Virginia residents.\par \par \uc2 Election Tuesday\par \par \uc2 More WSJ coverage, selected by the editors\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/virginia-governor-elections-what-to-know-11635800675"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 When to Expect the Virginia Results }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/nyc-mayoral-race-eric-adams-leads-polls-as-new-yorkers-vote-11635845400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Eric Adams Wins NYC Mayor Election }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/atlanta-boston-and-new-york-vote-for-new-mayors-11635897600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Atlanta Awaits Mayoral Outcome }}}\par \par \uc2 Chad Day, Jimmy Vielkind and Andrew Restuccia contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Scott Calvert at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:scott.calvert@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 scott.calvert@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Alexa Corse at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:alexa.corse@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alexa.corse@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/terry-mcauliffe-glenn-youngkin-in-dead-heat-in-virginia-governors-race-11635845400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Youngkin Takes Narrow Lead in Virginia Governor's Election }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020211102ehb2000xh\par }{\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
