\par\par \uc2 World News\par \uc2 World\par \b \uc2 Biden Says Pope Told Him He Is a Good Catholic Amid Controversy Over  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ; President, who supports  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights, says \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  told him to continue receiving Communion\b0\par\par\uc2 By Francis X. Rocca and Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 1,118 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 October 2021\par 16:51 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 VATICAN CITY\u8212\'20\'14President Biden, after meeting \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , said the pontiff told him to continue receiving Communion, amid {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pope-francis-faces-tests-on-abortion-gay-rights-11632913201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a controversy among U.S. church leaders }}}\uc2  over whether the president's support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bishops-vote-to-prepare-document-on-communion-for-catholic-politicians-who-support-abortion-rights-11624041010"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 should disqualify him from receiving the sacrament }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We just talked about the fact he was happy that I was a good Catholic and I should keep receiving Communion," Mr. Biden said. The Vatican didn't immediately reply to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-trump-catholic-voters-presidential-election-abortion-supreme-court-11600961731"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the second Catholic president in U.S. history }}}\uc2 , has come under fire from some U.S. bishops who say that Catholic politicians {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-reverse-abortion-rule-known-as-mexico-city-policy-11611835467"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 who support legal access to \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  should be barred from Communion. In a little more than two weeks, at their annual fall meeting in Baltimore, U.S. bishops are expected to debate whether to make a collective statement to that effect.\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , while reaffirming the church's condemnation of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has taken a more conciliatory approach toward the president and the Vatican has said that linking the politics of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the reception of Communion would be divisive.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden declined to say on Friday whether he and the pope had discussed the U.S. bishops' debate, saying "that's a private conversation."\par \par \uc2 A spokeswoman for the U.S. Conference of Catholic Bishops declined to comment on the president's remarks.\par \par \uc2 Neither the Vatican nor the White House mentioned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their summary statements after the leaders' meeting, a sign that neither party wanted the press the issue.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden thanked the pope for {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pope-says-fighting-abortion-and-poverty-are-equally-sacred-causes-1523268012"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 his work against poverty }}}\uc2  and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-is-cop26-glasgow-climate-change-11611254971"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 climate change }}}\uc2 , "as well as his advocacy to ensure the pandemic ends for everyone through vaccine sharing and an equitable global economic recovery," according to the White House.\par \par \uc2 The Vatican said they discussed the environment, the fight against Covid-19 and the plight of refugees and migrants\u8212\'20\'14all areas of broad agreement between the pope and president. The only possible hint of discord was a reference to "the protection of human rights, including freedom of religion and conscience."\par \par \uc2 U.S. Catholic bishops have criticized the Equality Act, proposed legislation supported by Mr. Biden that would expand antidiscrimination protections to cover sexual orientation and gender identity, which bishops say would infringe on the church's religious freedom.\par \par \uc2 After the meeting, Mr. Biden told reporters that his time with the pope had been wonderful.\par \par \uc2 The pope and Mr. Biden spoke in private for an unusually long 75 minutes. The pope typically meets with visiting heads of state for around half an hour, as he did with President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in 2017, though he spent more than 50 minutes with President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  in 2014.\par \par \uc2 It was the fourth meeting between the two men, who previously met when Mr. Biden was vice president: at the Vatican in 2013 and 2016 and during \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 ' 2015 visit to the U.S.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden has made his faith a prominent element of his public persona and placed a photo of the pope behind his desk in the Oval Office.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, whereas \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  in recent weeks has underscored the church's strong opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , describing it as murder and likening it to hiring a hit man to solve a problem. However, the pope has also warned bishops not to politicize the reception of Communion.\par \par \uc2 On Inauguration Day in January, Archbishop Jos\u233\'00\'E9 G\u243\'00\'F3mez of Los Angeles, president of the U.S. Conference of Catholic Bishops, said Mr. Biden "has pledged to pursue certain policies that would advance moral evils and threaten human life and dignity, most seriously in the areas of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , contraception, marriage and gender."\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2 , in a message to Mr. Biden the same day, didn't mention any of those issues.\par \par \uc2 During a meeting in June, some U.S. bishops said it was urgent to clarify the church's teaching on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under a Catholic president who supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. The bishops then voted 168 to 55, with six abstentions, for a document on the Eucharist that would address the question of eligibility to receive Communion. The latest draft of that document, which the bishops will vote on next month, doesn't include a statement that Catholic politicians who support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights should be barred from Communion, but bishops can propose amendments to the document up to and during next month's meeting.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 On what issues would you like to see President Biden and \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  work together? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The president regularly attends Mass and receives Communion. Cardinal \uc2 Wilton Gregory\uc2 , who as archbishop of Washington is the president's pastor, has said that he wouldn't refuse him the sacrament. Mr. Biden told reporters that he did not receive Communion during his visit to the Vatican on Friday.\par \par \uc2 Following this weekend's summit of leaders of the \uc2 Group of 20\uc2  major global economies in Rome, Mr. Biden will attend the United Nations climate summit, known as COP26, in Glasgow, Scotland, on Monday and Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  has made climate change a signature issue of his pontificate. In a radio message broadcast by the \uc2 British Broadcasting Corp\uc2 . on Friday, the pope called on participants at COP26 "to provide effective responses to the present ecological crisis and in this way to offer concrete hope to future generations."\par \par \uc2 Video images released by the Vatican after their private meeting showed the pope and president smiling and exchanging pleasantries. A White House official said "the engagement between the two was very warm\u8230\'20\'26There was laughter and clear rapport."\par \par \uc2 After the private meeting, the president was joined by first lady Jill Biden for an exchange of gifts with the pontiff. \uc2 Pope Francis\uc2  gave the president a painting on a ceramic tile depicting a pilgrim, along with several Vatican publications including a papal message on peace. Mr. Biden gave the pope a vintage liturgical vestment as well as a commemorative coin that he said he normally gives to warriors and leaders.\par \par \uc2 "You are the most significant warrior for peace I've ever met," Mr. Biden told the pope.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Controversy\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pope-francis-and-president-biden-to-meet-as-both-face-abortion-tensions-with-u-s-bishops-11635327000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pope Francis and President Biden to Meet as Both Face \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Tensions With U.S. Bishops }}}\uc2  (Oct. 27)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/pope-francis-faces-tests-on-abortion-gay-rights-11632913201"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pope Francis Faces Tests on \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 , Gay Rights }}}\uc2  (Sept. 29)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bishops-vote-to-prepare-document-on-communion-for-catholic-politicians-who-support-abortion-rights-11624041010"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Bishops Advance Effort That Could Restrict Communion for Biden }}}\uc2  (June 18)\par \par \uc2 Write to Francis X. Rocca at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:francis.rocca@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 francis.rocca@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-pope-francis-meet-amid-controversy-over-abortion-11635502337"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden Says Pope Told Him He Is a Good Catholic Amid Controversy Over \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020211029ehat000ul\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
