\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court Agrees to Quick Consideration of Texas  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law; Court leaves state law in place for now; it will hear oral arguments on Nov. 1\b0\par\par\uc2 By Brent Kendall \par \uc2 1,250 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 October 2021\par 21:38 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The Supreme Court on Friday agreed to quickly consider two lawsuits challenging a Texas ban on most abortions but left the restrictive law in place for now, adding a new blockbuster battle to a docket that already included another major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights case.\par \par \uc2 The court set oral arguments for Nov. 1 but deferred acting on an emergency request from the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/justice-departments-asks-supreme-court-to-block-texas-abortion-law-11634582218"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice Department to block the Texas law  }}}\uc2  while the federal government challenges its legality. The Texas limits, which are the most restrictive in the U.S., have been in effect for nearly two months.\par \par \uc2 The case adds more urgency to a Supreme Court term that already was shaping up to be a momentous one for the future of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. The justices in December will review {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-mississippi-abortion-case-supreme-court-sets-arguments-for-december-11632176939"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an appeal by the state of Mississippi  }}}\uc2 , which is seeking to implement an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Both states are seeking to roll back precedents protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, starting with the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision. The high court for years declined to entertain such requests, but Republican-led states have been more willing to test the issue after recent changes in the court's membership have made it more conservative.\par \par \uc2 "These are home-run swings by these states," said \uc2 University of Illinois\uc2  law-school dean Vikram Amar. "There's no way to uphold the Texas or Mississippi statutes absent dramatic changes in the existing doctrine and rules. And so, by the end of this term, we're going to know whether this is an incremental conservative court or a transformational one."\par \par \uc2 With Friday's action, the justices stepped into the Texas battle even though lower courts haven't issued final rulings on the law, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-in-court-what-you-need-to-know-11631730720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 known as the Texas Heartbeat Act  }}}\uc2 , or SB 8, which bars abortions after about six weeks of pregnancy. The measure limits the procedure far earlier than allowed by current Supreme Court precedent, which says that women have a constitutional right to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability. Doctors generally consider viability\u8212\'20\'14when a fetus could live outside the womb\u8212\'20\'14to fall around 21 to 24 weeks into a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Texas state Sen. \uc2 Bryan Hughes\uc2  , the Republican author of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, said: "I am encouraged that the law will remain in effect while the case is before the court, and I am optimistic that the court will uphold the right of Texans to protect life."\par \par \uc2 The law's critics voiced mixed views on Friday's developments.\par \par \uc2 "It's good in the sense that we may get an answer more quickly than we would have otherwise," said Texas state Rep. Donna Howard , a Democrat who chairs the Texas Women's Health Caucus. But it was disappointing, she added, that "Texas women are still being denied the rights and protections that every other U.S. woman has while this is going on."\par \par \uc2 The high court said it would hear separate appeals by the Justice Department and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers to decide legal issues related to Texas's novel effort to shield its law from federal-court review.\par \par \uc2 The court's latest order comes weeks after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 it voted 5-4 on Sept. 1 to let the Texas law go into effect  }}}\uc2 . The justices' prior order came when it denied an emergency appeal by the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers, with the court's majority saying there were procedural problems with how they sued to challenge the law.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department stepped in days later with its own lawsuit against Texas and argued its claims didn't face the same hurdles that prevented the high court from intervening in the providers' case.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, a federal judge in Austin sided with the department and granted a preliminary injunction blocking the law, but the Fifth Circuit Court of Appeals last week put that ruling on hold, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-restrictions-can-continue-during-litigation-appeals-court-rules-11634261230"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowing the state restrictions to remain in force for now.  }}}\par \par \uc2 Under SB 8, physicians can't perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if they know there is "a detectable fetal heartbeat," which the law defines as including cardiac activity in the embryo in the early weeks of pregnancy. The law doesn't contain exceptions for rape or incest.\par \par \uc2 Texas wrote its law in a manner designed to make it difficult to challenge in court, by preventing state officials from having any direct role in enforcing the law. Instead, SB 8 empowers private parties to file civil lawsuits alleging violations. A plaintiff who wins in court can collect at least $10,000 from someone found to have performed\u8212\'20\'14or aided\u8212\'20\'14a banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 During the weeks since the law took effect, abortions have been difficult to obtain in Texas, with some women traveling to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in neighboring states.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department, in papers filed with the Supreme Court, said Texas was openly defying federal constitutional law and had "successfully nullified this court's decisions within its borders."\par \par \uc2 If the state's tactics succeed, there is nothing to stop other states from writing laws that deny other constitutional rights the Supreme Court has previously protected, such as the right to own a handgun in the home, the department said.\par \par \uc2 Texas in response said it was under no obligation to make its law easy to challenge and argued the Justice Department's lawsuit was improper.\par \par \uc2 "The federal government cannot get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the Constitution does not assign it any special role to protect any putative right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the state wrote in a court brief.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court on Friday said it would decide whether the federal government can sue Texas in federal court and obtain a ruling "against the state, state court judges, state court clerks, other state officials, or all private parties to prohibit SB 8 from being enforced."\par \par \uc2 In the providers' case, the court will be considering whether Texas can insulate its law from federal-court review by delegating enforcement authority to the general public.\par \par \uc2 Under the Supreme Court's normal timelines, rulings would be expected by the end of next June, though the decisions could come earlier since the justices are treating the cases in expedited fashion.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  , writing separately on Friday, criticized the court for not blocking the law immediately while it considers the cases.\par \par \uc2 "The promise of future adjudication offers cold comfort\u8230\'20\'26for Texas women seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, who are entitled to relief now," Justice Sotomayor wrote. "These women will suffer personal harm from delaying their medical care, and as their pregnancies progress, they may even be unable to obtain \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  care altogether."\par \par \uc2 Despite the fast-moving Texas proceedings, the Mississippi case, set for arguments Dec. 1, still may be the one in which the Supreme Court addresses \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights issues more broadly.\par \par \uc2 Mississippi argues that nothing in the text, structure or history of the Constitution supports a right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . States, it says, have legitimate interests in preventing abortions well before fetal viability, which the 1973 court defined as the capability of meaningful life outside the mother's womb.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates say the state is pushing for radical changes in the law that would upend 50 years of practice and take away a woman's liberty in deciding whether to continue with a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Elizabeth Findell contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Brent Kendall at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:brent.kendall@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brent.kendall@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-agrees-to-quick-consideration-of-texas-abortion-case-leaves-state-law-in-place-for-now-11634921299"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court Agrees to Quick Consideration of Texas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020211022eham004v1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
