\par\par \uc2 Health Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 New Rule Ends Ban on Federal Funds for Clinics That Refer Abortions; The decision reverses an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  policy under the Trump administration\b0\par\par\uc2 By Tarini Parti \par \uc2 554 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2021\par 00:27 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The Biden administration Monday reversed a Trump-era policy that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-administration-curbs-federal-funding-for-clinics-providing-abortions-11550866834"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stripped federal family-planning dollars from clinics }}}\uc2  that refer patients for abortions.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  finalized a rule that would undo a 2019 policy on a federal program which called for clinics that received federal funding to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-administration-to-propose-denying-funds-to-clinics-that-refer-for-abortion-1526651330"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 physically separate their \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  services }}}\uc2  in a different building from all other services, and not to discuss abortions as an option with patients. The program, known as Title X, offers about $286 million each year to clinics that provide reproductive healthcare and other women's health screenings, such as Pap smears, to about four million uninsured Americans a year.\par \par \uc2 The new rule takes effect Nov. 8.\par \par \uc2 "This rule is a step forward for family planning care as it aims to strengthen and restore our nation's Title X program," said HHS Secretary \uc2 Xavier Becerra\uc2 . "Our nation's family planning clinics play a critical role in delivering health care, and today more than ever, we are making clear that access to quality family planning care includes accurate information and referrals\u8212\'20\'14based on a patient's needs and direction."\par \par \uc2 The ruling comes as the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-opens-new-term-with-masks-and-in-person-arguments-11633262400"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 returned to the courtroom }}}\uc2  Monday and is expected to take up a challenge to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights after declining to block a restrictive Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law that limits the procedure to the first six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-administration-proposes-reversing-ban-on-federal-funds-for-clinics-that-refer-abortions-11618422917"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took initial steps to undo the Trump administration policy }}}\uc2  in April.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters called the Trump-era policy a "gag rule" because they said it prevented doctors and other healthcare professionals from presenting patients with all available family-planning options. They argued that by pushing family planning clinics out of the federal network where uninsured women could receive family-planning services, the Trump administration also cut off access for women in many underserved communities where \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  is the only provider offering birth control and other women's healthcare.\par \par \uc2 "The end of the Title X gag rule is a major victory for patients, access to sexual and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care, and health equity," said \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2 , president and CEO of Planned Parenthood Federation of America, in a statement Monday. "Title X is a critical piece of our social safety net that can, and should, ensure that people with low incomes can access essential health care without forcing providers to withhold referrals for all of the options available to them."\par \par \uc2 The change under the Trump administration was one of a series of steps the former president took to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-administration-moves-on-abortion-cheer-antiabortion-movement-1505505209"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut funds for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  providers }}}\uc2 , a top concern for religious conservatives, who were a key part of former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's base and who shaped many aspects of his healthcare policy.\par \par \uc2 Federal dollars have long been prohibited by law from directly funding abortions, though advocates who oppose the procedure say funding to providers like \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , even for other services, essentially subsidizes them and makes it easier for \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  and other clinics to provide abortions.\par \par \uc2 Michelle Hackman contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Tarini Parti at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:Tarini.Parti@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Tarini.Parti@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/new-rule-ends-ban-on-federal-funds-for-clinics-that-refer-abortions-11633393632"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New Rule Ends Ban on Federal Funds for Clinics That Refer Abortions }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020211005eha50002t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
