\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Federal Judge Questions Texas  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law in Case Filed by Justice Department; State law, in effect for a month, has prompted some women to go to nearby states for the procedure\b0\par\par\uc2 By Brent Kendall \par \uc2 663 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 October 2021\par 18:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A federal judge Friday questioned Texas's defense of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-takes-effect-pending-supreme-court-action-11630498466?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 new \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law }}}\uc2  that is the most restrictive in the U.S. and which has significantly limited the procedure in the state.\par \par \uc2 U.S. District Judge Robert Pitman in Austin held a three-hour virtual hearing on a request by the Justice Department to block the law, which bans abortions after about the sixth week of pregnancy\u8212\'20\'14far sooner than current Supreme Court precedent allows and sometimes before a woman realizes she is pregnant.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think the Texas law banning most abortions is constitutional? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Known as the Texas Heartbeat Act, or SB 8, the law bars physicians from knowingly performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there is detectable embryonic cardiac activity. Texas lawmakers designed the measure so that it would be difficult to challenge in court by barring state officials from enforcing the law. Instead, the law delegates enforcement to private parties and authorizes civil damages of $10,000 or more to anyone who successfully sues a defendant accused of performing or aiding in such an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Judge Pitman, appointed by President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2 , questioned why the state went "to such great lengths" to create what he said was an unusual law aimed at hindering judicial review. "That's what the whole statute was designed to do," he said.\par \par \uc2 Lawyer Will Thompson, representing Texas, said there was nothing unprecedented about a state empowering private individuals to enforce a state law in state courts.\par \par \uc2 Under questioning from the judge, Mr. Thompson said it wasn't possible for the judge to issue a workable injunction because there was no person that the court could validly prohibit from enforcing the law.\par \par \uc2 Judge Pitman, however, sent signals that he may try, asking several questions that mused on what a potential injunction against the law could look like. He didn't say when he would issue a ruling.\par \par \uc2 The law has been in effect for a month. The Supreme Court, by a 5-4 vote, on Sept. 1 declined an emergency request by \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers that asked the justices to intervene and halt the measure. The high court's majority said there were procedural reasons that prevented it from potentially blocking the law. In the weeks since, SB 8 has prevented many abortions in the state, with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-prompts-women-to-seek-out-of-state-clinics-11632315616"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 some women traveling to out-of-state clinics }}}\uc2  to obtain the procedure.\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department stepped in with a lawsuit Sept. 9, arguing Texas had adopted a near-ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  that was in open defiance of the Constitution. It {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/justice-department-asks-federal-judge-to-quickly-block-texas-abortion-law-11631684768"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 asked for the law to be put on hold }}}\uc2  while its litigation moves forward. The department argued that the procedural complications in the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers' lawsuit weren't applicable to the federal government's case.\par \par \uc2 Texas has resorted to a "scheme of vigilante justice" that denies constitutionally protected \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and is "an open threat to the rule of law," Justice Department lawyer Brian Netter argued Friday. The state, he said, had engaged in "an unprecedented attack on the supremacy of the federal government."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Thompson said the department's arguments were filled with "hyperbole and inflammatory rhetoric." He argued the federal government had no valid basis for bringing the lawsuit.\par \par \uc2 Judge Pitman directed most of his questions during the hearing to Texas, though he did ask the Justice Department whether there were limits on the federal government's ability to directly sue a state in an effort to block one of its laws.\par \par \uc2 Separate from the federal litigation, there are other proceedings in state court, including lawsuits against a doctor who recently said he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-doctor-who-performed-abortion-is-sued-in-test-of-new-law-11632176035?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 performed an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\uc2  in violation of the Texas law.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/federal-judge-questions-texas-abortion-law-in-case-filed-by-justice-department-11633112921"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Federal Judge Questions Texas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law in Case Filed by Justice Department }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020211001eha1006el\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
