\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 House Passes Bill to Protect  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights, Countering Texas Restrictions; Bill, which would stop states from imposing curbs before fetal viability, is unlikely to advance in the Senate\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins \par \uc2 670 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 September 2021\par 17:26 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The House passed legislation on Friday that would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions before fetal viability, a response by Democrats to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-in-court-what-you-need-to-know-11631730720"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a recently enacted Texas law  }}}\uc2  that bans the procedure after about six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The Women's Health Protection Act would stop states from enacting restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability. It would also halt requirements for tests or procedures, such as ultrasounds, that are deemed medically unnecessary before abortions. Doctors generally consider viability\u8212\'20\'14when a fetus could live outside the womb\u8212\'20\'14to fall around 21 to 24 weeks into a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The bill passed 218-211, mostly along party lines, with one Democrat, Rep. \uc2 Henry Cuellar\uc2  of Texas, joining Republicans in voting against it. The proposal is unlikely to advance in the evenly divided Senate, where it would require 10 Republicans to join with all Democrats for passage. Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D., N.Y.) is expected to bring the legislation up for a vote in the near future, according to a Democratic aide.\par \par \uc2 "Every day women in our country face deeply personal decisions of whether to continue their pregnancies, they should be able to make their own decisions, free from politicians interference. The Women's Health Protection Act is exactly that," said Rep. \uc2 Anna Eshoo\uc2  (D., Calif.) ahead of the vote Friday.\par \par \uc2 Republicans were united in their opposition.\par \par \uc2 The legislation "isn't about freedom for women, it's about death for babies," said Rep. \uc2 Vicky Hartzler\uc2  (R., Mo.).\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the Supreme Court, in a 5-4 decision, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to block the new Texas law  }}}\uc2 , rejecting an emergency request by clinics and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates. The law bans abortions after "cardiac activity" can be detected, usually around six weeks of gestation, and it deputizes private citizens to sue anyone they believe may have aided such a procedure.\par \par \uc2 While not a final ruling on the measure's constitutionality, both proponents and opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions said the court's decision marked a turning point in the legal battle over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, potentially putting the issue on the front burner in coming elections to determine control of Congress and the White House.\par \par \uc2 House Democrats say their bill would codify into law the Supreme Court's 1973 Roe v. Wade decision, which established the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  under the Constitution.\par \par \uc2 The current split over the issue in Congress shows just how {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-republicans-now-unanimous-in-opposing-abortion-rights-11553172954"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 partisan the \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  debate  }}}\uc2  has become. In 2019, the last two pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights Republicans in the House retired. In 2020, one of the last remaining antiabortion Democrats {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/marie-newman-defeats-rep-dan-lipinski-in-illinois-primary-challenge-11584507001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost his primary  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Sen. \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine, a Republican, identifies as pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights and said she supports codifying Roe into law. However, Ms. Collins said she wouldn't support this legislation if it came up in the Senate because she believes it goes beyond just making the Supreme Court decision law. In particular, she said the bill would "severely weaken protections afforded to healthcare providers who refuse to perform abortions on religious or moral grounds."\par \par \uc2 Ms. Collins said she is working with Senate Democratic colleagues on an alternative, but didn't specify which lawmakers.\par \par \uc2 Alaska Sen. \uc2 Lisa Murkowski\uc2  , the other pro-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights Republican, hasn't decided how she will vote, a spokeswoman said.\par \par \uc2 In addition, it isn't clear if Democratic senators would be united on the legislation. Sens. Bob Casey of Pennsylvania and Joe Manchin of West Virginia have declined to co-sponsor the Senate version of the legislation. A spokeswoman for Mr. Manchin said he hasn't said how he would vote. A representative for Mr. Casey didn't immediately respond to a request for comment on how he would vote if the matter came to the Senate floor.\par \par \uc2 Write to Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins+1@wsj.com."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins+1@wsj.com.  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/house-to-vote-on-abortion-rights-measure-to-counter-texas-restrictions-11632493817"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 House Passes Bill to Protect \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rights, Countering Texas Restrictions  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210924eh9o003jt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
