\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 In Mississippi  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Case, Supreme Court Sets Arguments for December; Opponents and defenders of  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  rights weigh in on landmark challenge to Roe v. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jess Bravin \par \uc2 615 \uc2 words\par \uc2 20 September 2021\par 22:28 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  set Dec. 1 for arguments over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-consider-abortion-restrictions-from-mississippi-11621259099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a Mississippi law  }}}\uc2  banning most abortions after 15 weeks, a case that could bring the court's most significant ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the Roe v. Wade decision in 1973.\par \par \uc2 The court announced the date on Monday, as dozens of organizations, officials and advocates submitted briefs seeking to influence the decision before a midnight filing deadline. While many positions were predictable\u8212\'20\'14the \uc2 National Right to Life Committee\uc2  favoring the ban, \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  in opposition\u8212\'20\'14the case drew a range of submissions from around the world.\par \par \uc2 More than 500 female athletes, including Olympic, national and collegiate champions, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/athletebrief.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed a brief  }}}\uc2  arguing that the availability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been essential to the growth of women's sports since the 1970s.\par \par \uc2 "When I was in college, I was on birth control, but I accidentally became pregnant," wrote Crissy Perham, who won three swimming medals at the 1992 Barcelona Olympics.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Perham, then studying at the \uc2 University of Arizona\uc2  , wrote that ending her pregnancy allowed her "to take control of my future and refocus my priorities. I got better in school, I started training really hard, and that summer, I won my first national championship."\par \par \uc2 On the other side, two scholars who have shaped modern conservative thought filed a brief arguing that "a distinct human being begins at conception," and therefore \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be considered homicide.\par \par \uc2 John Finnis, who was an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/gorsuch-has-strong-tie-to-proponent-of-morality-based-natural-law-1489610561"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 academic adviser  }}}\uc2  to Justice \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  at Britain's \uc2 Oxford University\uc2  , and Robert George of \uc2 Princeton University\uc2  cite historical and religious treatises to argue that the framers would have held similar views.\par \par \uc2 "The influential and widely circulated 1803 textbook 'Medical Ethics' explained that 'to extinguish the first spark of life is a crime of the same nature, both against our maker and society, as to destroy an infant, a child, or a man,'" the professors wrote.\par \par \uc2 Lower courts have blocked the Mississippi Gestational Age Act, or HB 1510, for running headlong into both Roe and Planned Parenthood v. Casey, a 1992 precedent that narrowed but didn't eliminate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 "This law is facially unconstitutional because it directly conflicts with Casey," which prohibits officials from imposing undue burdens on women who wish to end pregnancies before fetal viability, the New Orleans-based Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals said in December 2019.\par \par \uc2 Mississippi argues, in its case, that the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  should overrule precedents that conflict with its statute. "This case is made hard only because Roe v. Wade and Planned Parenthood of Southeastern Pennsylvania v. Casey hold that the Constitution protects a right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the state's brief says.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  voted 5-4 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to permit a Texas law  }}}\uc2  banning abortions after about six weeks to take effect; the majority, including the court's most conservative members, said that federal courts lacked power to review the law at that stage because it assigned enforcement power to private parties that filed civil lawsuits rather than state officials. The court said its decision should be considered procedural and not a pronouncement on the viability of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  and three more liberal justices dissented, arguing that the Texas's civil enforcement mechanism, which advocates have said was designed to deflect legal challenges, shouldn't prevent the court from reviewing a measure with significant constitutional implications.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jess.bravin+1@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jess.bravin+1@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/in-mississippi-abortion-case-supreme-court-sets-arguments-for-december-11632176939"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In Mississippi \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Case, Supreme Court Sets Arguments for December  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210920eh9k005xx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
