\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Judge Sets Oct. 1 Hearing for Federal Bid to Block Texas  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law; Justice Department seeks a preliminary injunction or temporary restraining order while court considers department's lawsuit against Texas\b0\par\par\uc2 By Brent Kendall and Jess Bravin \par \uc2 704 \uc2 words\par \uc2 15 September 2021\par 05:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14A federal judge set an Oct. 1 hearing date for the Biden administration's bid to block a Texas law designed to largely end access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout the state.\par \par \uc2 Late Tuesday, the Justice Department asked U.S. District Judge Robert Pitman, in Austin, Texas, for an emergency order that effectively would nullify the Texas Heartbeat Act, or SB 8, which bans abortions after about six weeks. The judge gave Texas until Sept. 29 to file its written response.\par \par \uc2 That schedule allows SB 8 to remain in effect for at least another two weeks, even though its substance conflicts with current Supreme Court precedents, which limit restrictions of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  prior to fetal viability. But SB 8 employs an unusual procedural mechanism devised to frustrate court review, authorizing private parties to sue \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers rather than relying on state officials to enforce the law.\par \par \uc2 Earlier this month, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 5-4 Supreme Court }}}\uc2  said that feature tied its hands after \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers asked the justices to block the law. Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  and three more-liberal justices dissented, saying the law should have been placed on hold while the court examined the measure and its unique enforcement structure.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-administration-expected-to-file-suit-soon-challenging-texas-abortion-law-11631205764"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Justice Department then sued Texas }}}\uc2 , arguing that SB 8 interfered with several federal programs as well as denying women a constitutional right the Supreme Court has recognized since the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 "This relief is necessary to protect the constitutional rights of women in Texas and the sovereign interest of the United States in ensuring that its states respect the terms of the national compact," the department's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://storage.courtlistener.com/recap/gov.uscourts.txwd.1146510/gov.uscourts.txwd.1146510.6.1.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 emergency motion }}}\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 The state measure, which went into effect on Sept. 1, bars physicians from knowingly performing an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there is "a detectable fetal heartbeat," including embryonic cardiac activity that appears about six weeks into a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 SB 8 authorizes damages of $10,000 or more to anyone who successfully sues a defendant accused of performing or aiding in an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In legal papers, the Justice Department said the procedural hurdles that might interfere with a private plaintiff's suit weren't applicable to the federal government.\par \par \uc2 Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , in announcing the Justice Department lawsuit last week, accused Texas of engaging in a scheme "to nullify the Constitution."\par \par \uc2 The department announced last week that it would be requesting the kind of preliminary relief that it formally sought with Tuesday's emergency motion.\par \par \uc2 The office of Texas Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  didn't respond to a request for comment. Previously, Mr. Paxton said the Biden administration should focus on other priorities "instead of meddling in states' sovereign rights."\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department filing Tuesday asserted that the Texas Heartbeat Act, or SB 8, has already all but eliminated access to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the state.\par \par \uc2 "Due to the prospect of ruinous liability for clinics and providers, beginning September 1, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in Texas ceased providing abortions after six weeks, absent a medical emergency, which likely amounts to between 85 and 95% of all abortions previously provided," the department said.\par \par \uc2 In deciding whether to issue an injunction, judges are required to balance various factors, including the likelihood of each party's ultimate success and the harms that each side might suffer. The Justice Department argued that SB 8 harmed both individual women and various federal policies that provide abortions to federal prison inmates, service members and others, while Texas had no interest in enforcement of a law that is unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 "The clear purpose and effect of S.B. 8 is to deny women rights guaranteed to them by the U.S. Constitution, while attempting to evade judicial review,'' the government said. "Texas plainly lacks any legitimate interest in that impermissible objective, and it has no valid interest in insulating its unconstitutional laws from judicial review."\par \par \uc2 Write to Brent Kendall at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:brent.kendall@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brent.kendall@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jess.bravin@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jess.bravin@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/justice-department-asks-federal-judge-to-quickly-block-texas-abortion-law-11631684768"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Judge Sets Oct. 1 Hearing for Federal Bid to Block Texas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210915eh9f000p1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
