\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Biden Administration Sues Texas Over Its  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law; Lawsuit targets state law limiting procedure to first six weeks of pregnancy\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sadie Gurman and Brent Kendall \par \uc2 1,376 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 September 2021\par 16:17 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The Justice Department sued Texas Thursday to block {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a new state law banning most abortions  }}}\uc2 , saying it was enacted "in open defiance of the Constitution."\par \par \uc2 "This kind of scheme to nullify the Constitution of the United States is one that all Americans, whatever their politics or party, should fear," Attorney General \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  said at a news conference announcing the action.\par \par \uc2 The case sets up a federal-state clash over {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-abortion-ruling-brings-new-uncertainty-to-decades-old-fight-11630621820"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the future of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights  }}}\uc2 , and a test of whether the department can upend a state law that Texas lawmakers drafted in a novel manner that makes it difficult for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates to challenge the ban in court.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law dictates that a physician can't knowingly perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there is "a detectable fetal heartbeat," including embryonic cardiac activity that appears about six weeks into a pregnancy. A provision of the law assigns enforcement to private parties, rather than state or local officials, and authorizes damages of $10,000 or more to anyone who successfully sues a defendant accused of performing or aiding in such an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 By putting enforcement powers in the hands of private citizens, rather than state or local officials, the Texas law has left its opponents without obvious individuals to sue.\par \par \uc2 "The obvious and expressly acknowledged intention of this statutory scheme is to prevent women from exercising their constitutional rights by thwarting judicial review for as long as possible," Mr. Garland said.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/DOJ Texas lawsuit.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The suit  }}}\uc2 , filed in federal court in Austin, said the federal government "has the authority and responsibility" to ensure that Texas doesn't deprive individuals of their constitutional rights by attempting to evade the courts. It seeks a preliminary injunction to block the law while litigation continues, as well as a permanent order that the Texas ban is invalid and unenforceable.\par \par \uc2 Texas Gov. Greg Abbott defended the state law and called the Biden administration's action a politically motivated distraction.\par \par \uc2 "Texas passed a law that ensures that the life of every child with a heartbeat will be spared from the ravages of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said a spokeswoman for the Republican governor. "We are confident that the courts will uphold and protect that right to life."\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department alleged the Texas ban violates the Constitution's Supremacy Clause, which commands that federal law is supreme to state law, as well as the 14th Amendment's guarantee of due process of law, the basis for the Supreme Court's recognition of a constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The further risk here is that other states will follow similar models with respect not only to this constitutional right but, theoretically, against any constitutional right," Mr. Garland said, warning that the Justice Department could take similar action against other states.\par \par \uc2 The department also alleged the state measure was pre-empted by federal law because it prohibited certain abortions "that federal agencies are charged with facilitating, funding, or reimbursing," including through healthcare programs that cover the procedure in cases of rape or incest. The Texas law includes no exceptions for such cases.\par \par \uc2 The ban puts the Health, Defense and Labor departments in legal jeopardy for carrying out \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -related services, the suit said.\par \par \uc2 Share your thoughts\par \par \uc2 Do you think the Texas law banning most abortions is constitutional? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 While the Texas ban is in clear conflict with current Supreme Court precedent, the Justice Department may face other challenges to securing a favorable ruling.\par \par \uc2 The department, for example, could be hard-pressed to demonstrate it has the ability to sue on behalf of women in Texas, said Mary Ziegler, a law professor at \uc2 Florida State University\uc2  . She suggested the department could be considering other legal tools to fight the law, such as whether federal civil-rights law could apply.\par \par \uc2 "This is probably not the last thing we hear from the Biden administration, even if this is going to face some procedural obstacles," she said.\par \par \uc2 After originally being assigned to another judge, the case was reassigned late Thursday to U.S. District Judge \uc2 Robert Pitman\uc2  , an Obama appointee who presided over earlier litigation in which \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers challenged the Texas ban. The judge denied requests to dismiss the providers' claims and scheduled a hearing last month on whether to block the law, but an appeals court put those proceedings on hold, preventing him from issuing a ruling.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court let the Texas law go into effect last week after a majority of justices found no basis for the court to intervene, despite what they said were serious questions about the law's constitutionality.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration had faced pressure from Democrats and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups to take action to stop the Texas law after the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283?mod=hp_lead_pos1&mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 allowed it to take effect  }}}\uc2 , sending \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers and patients scrambling.\par \par \uc2 President Biden last week pledged a "whole-of-government effort" to respond to the Supreme Court's order allowing the Texas law to stand, and said he asked the Justice Department to explore ways to challenge it.\par \par \uc2 House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) said {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-house-vote-planned-by-pelosi-after-supreme-court-decision-11630603877"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the chamber would vote later this month  }}}\uc2  on legislation to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights by banning restrictions before fetal viability. The legislation is unlikely to pass the evenly divided Senate, where it would need 60 votes. Senate Majority Leader \uc2 Chuck Schumer\uc2  (D., N.Y.) hasn't announced a pending vote.\par \par \uc2 Other Democrats in Congress this week urged Mr. Garland to prosecute Texas residents who try under the new law to sue women seeking abortions.\par \par \uc2 "The Department of Justice cannot permit private individuals seeking to deprive women of the constitutional right to choose an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to escape scrutiny under existing federal law simply because they attempt to do so under the color of state law," Democrats on the \uc2 House Judiciary Committee\uc2  said Tuesday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://judiciary.house.gov/uploadedfiles/2021-09-07_hjc_dems_to_ag_garland.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a letter to Mr. Garland  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents and Republican lawmakers have hailed the law as a model for reversing the viability standard established by Roe v. Wade and subsequent Supreme Court decisions. "The Supreme Court just let Texas's pro-life law go into effect, saving countless innocent lives," tweeted Sen. Tom Cotton (R., Ark.), who is seen as a potential 2024 presidential candidate. "Why stop there? The Court should let every state set its own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws by overturning Roe v Wade."\par \par \uc2 The Justice Department has previously said it would be stepping up prosecutions of people who injure or intimidate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -clinic patients and employees under a federal law known as the 1994 Freedom of Access to Clinic Entrances Act, a statute that has been described as spottily enforced in the past. Mr. Garland said Monday the department had reached out to the \uc2 Federal Bureau of Investigation\uc2  and federal prosecutors across Texas to discuss how to enforce that law.\par \par \uc2 The Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law sets no limit on how much money those who sue to challenge abortions can recover. If they prevail, they can also demand that the losing party pay their legal bills. If they lose in court and their case is dismissed, they owe the defendant nothing.\par \par \uc2 The law permits several lawsuits to be filed by different individuals over a single \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Once a claimant collects damages, though, the others suing may not collect more money from the same defendant for the same violation.\par \par \uc2 In allowing the Texas law to take effect, the Supreme Court didn't rule on the measure's constitutionality. The Justice Department's new lawsuit could join legal challenges on the state level that seek to give courts a better opportunity to rule on the ban's validity.\par \par \uc2 In its next session, the Supreme Court is already slated to rule on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mississippi-asks-supreme-court-to-end-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-11626985810?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi's law  }}}\uc2  banning most abortions after 15 weeks, with the state arguing for an abolition of federal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Lower federal courts have blocked that law for violating Supreme Court precedent. A ruling in that case is expected by next summer.\par \par \uc2 Kris Maher contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Sadie Gurman at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:sadie.gurman@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 sadie.gurman@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Brent Kendall at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:brent.kendall@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brent.kendall@wsj.com  }}}\uc2  and Brent Kendall at\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-administration-expected-to-file-suit-soon-challenging-texas-abortion-law-11631205764"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden Administration Sues Texas Over Its \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210909eh990040h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
