\par\par \uc2 Review & Outlook (U.S.)\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Kavanaugh to the Liberal Rescue; Democrats discover that a private right of action without injury is unfair.\b0\par\par\uc2 By The Editorial Board \par \uc2 446 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 September 2021\par 21:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Democrats are up in arms over a Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law they say creates a "vigilante system" by deputizing private citizens to enforce it. What do you know, they seem to have discovered the wisdom of the Supreme Court conservatives who recently limited vigilantism by plaintiff attorneys in federal courts.\par \par \uc2 In TransUnion v. Ramirez (2021), 6,332 plaintiffs sued the credit agency \uc2 TransUnion\uc2  for failing to cross-check information in their files. The Fair Credit Reporting Act includes what's known as a private right of action that allows consumers to sue credit agencies for violating the law and receive damages if they prevail.\par \par \uc2 But under the Court's precedents, plaintiffs must show they suffered a concrete and particularized injury to sue. Five Justices ruled that the plaintiffs lacked legal standing to sue in federal court because they had not been concretely harmed by \uc2 TransUnion\uc2  's lapses.\par \par \uc2 "The Court has rejected the proposition that 'a plaintiff automatically satisfies the injury-in-fact requirement whenever a statute grants a person a statutory right and purports to authorize that person to sue to vindicate that right,'" Justice \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  wrote for the majority, citing the Court's \uc2 Spokeo\uc2  decision (2016).\par \par \uc2 "A regime where Congress could freely authorize unharmed plaintiffs to sue defendants who violate federal law not only would violate Article III but also would infringe on the Executive Branch's Article II authority," {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/opinions/20pdf/20-297_4g25.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he added }}}\uc2 . "Private plaintiffs are not accountable to the people and are not charged with pursuing the public interest in enforcing a defendant's general compliance with regulatory law."\par \par \uc2 The decision was important because it reinforced that plaintiffs must show they are both personally and concretely harmed to sue in federal court. Liberals argue that the mere establishment of a private right of action should be sufficient, as it is in Texas's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. Under Texas's law, a private citizen can sue someone who aids or abets an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  after six weeks and receive at least $10,000 in damages per \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and legal costs.Texas's law authorizes private lawsuits in state courts, so \uc2 TransUnion\uc2  doesn't directly apply. But the law is a prototype of the legal vigilante system many liberals want to create to target businesses.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court last week {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-blunder-supreme-court-samuel-alito-john-roberts-whole-womans-health-11630619631"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 declined to block }}}\uc2  the Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law for sound procedural reasons. But the law is likely to be struck down as unconstitutional when courts consider the merits. Perhaps Democrats will then recognize the wisdom of strictly enforcing the Court's standing principles.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/brett-kavanaugh-to-the-texas-rescue-transunion-supreme-court-abortion-law-11630939967"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Kavanaugh to the Liberal Rescue }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210906eh96003h2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
