\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Pelosi Plans  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Rights Vote for House After Supreme Court's Texas Decision; Legislation has limited prospects in Congress but could highlight the issue headed into midterm elections\b0\par\par\uc2 By Eliza Collins and Aaron Zitner \par \uc2 1,348 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2021\par 21:02 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14House Speaker \uc2 Nancy Pelosi\uc2  (D., Calif.) said the House would vote later this month on legislation designed to protect \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, following {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Supreme Court's decision to leave in place a new Texas law }}}\uc2  that bars the procedure after about six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The move sets up a contentious vote for the fall, while underscoring the limited prospects for congressional action related to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , an issue that has long divided Democrats and Republicans. The developments could also put the fight over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and restrictions at center stage as voters decide control of Congress in next year's midterms.\par \par \uc2 "The Supreme Court's cowardly, dark-of-night decision to uphold a flagrantly unconstitutional assault on women's rights and health is staggering," Mrs. Pelosi said. She said the court's action "necessitates codifying Roe v. Wade." Roe v. Wade is the 1973 ruling that recognized \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a woman's constitutional right.\par \par \uc2 Among other measures, the Women's Health Protection Act backed by Mrs. Pelosi would ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions before fetal viability.\par \par \uc2 The legislation could pass the Democratic-controlled House with a simple majority, if the party remains united. But its path in the Senate is more difficult, where a 60-vote filibuster threshold means Democrats would need to be united and bring on 10 Republicans to advance the bill, an unlikely outcome.\par \par \uc2 A spokesman for Senate Majority Leader Chuck Schumer (D., N.Y.) didn't immediately respond to a request for an update on the Senate's plans.\par \par \uc2 Other Democratic bills, including {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/democrats-reboot-stalled-election-law-push-11628275581"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 legislation on election rules }}}\uc2  and D.C. statehood, have passed the House but stalled in the 50-50 Senate, fueling calls by some Democratic lawmakers to eliminate the filibuster and let all legislation move with a simple majority. Some reiterated those demands Thursday as they pointed to the court's \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ruling.\par \par \uc2 "It's a more urgent reason to abolish or clearly reform the filibuster because we're dealing here with an issue of fundamental health and moral conscience," said Sen. Richard Blumenthal (D., Conn.) who is the lead sponsor of the Women's Health Protection Act in the Senate.\par \par \uc2 Several Democratic senators have firmly rejected the idea of eliminating the filibuster, leaving the effort short of the majority needed to change chamber rules. President Biden has said he would be open to changes to the filibuster but doesn't support ending it altogether.\par \par \uc2 Late Wednesday the Supreme Court, in a 5-4 decision, declined to block a new Texas law that bars the procedure after about six weeks of pregnancy. The justices rejected an emergency request by clinics and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates the day the Texas ban went into force.\par \par \uc2 While not a final ruling on the measure's constitutionality, both proponents and opponents of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions said the court's decision marked a turning point in the legal battle over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, potentially putting the issue on the front burner in coming elections to determine control of Congress and the White House.\par \par \uc2 "The Supreme Court just let Texas's pro-life law go into effect, saving countless innocent lives," tweeted Sen. Tom Cotton (R., Ark.), seen as a potential 2024 presidential candidate. "Why stop there? The Court should let every state set its own \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws by overturning Roe v Wade."\par \par \uc2 The Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Law\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court Declines to Block Restrictive Texas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-new-texas-abortion-ban-law-takes-effect-providers-rush-to-adjust-11630521388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As New Texas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban Takes Effect, Providers Rush to Adjust }}}\par \par \uc2 On the other side of the aisle, several Democratic senators facing tough re-elections in the 2022 midterms, including Sens. \uc2 Catherine Cortez Masto\uc2  of Nevada and Mark Kelly of Arizona, issued statements backing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 The Texas law quickly became an issue in the marquee election contest of 2021, the race for governor in Virginia. Democratic nominee \uc2 Terry McAuliffe\uc2  told a business luncheon Wednesday that the Texas law offered a preview of what could happen in Virginia if his opponent, Republican Glenn Youngkin, were elected. Mr. McAuliffe returned to the subject on Thursday, telling reporters that ''there is a good chance we will see Virginia go the way of Texas, and women will lose their rights.''\par \par \uc2 Mr. Youngkin, interviewed by a reporter at the Wednesday luncheon, wouldn't say whether he would sign a law like the one in Texas and said his main concern was Mr. McAuliffe's position, which he described as favoring taxpayer-funded \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Some pollsters said they expected that the new state limits on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the potential for the Supreme Court to limit or overturn Roe v. Wade, would boost voter turnout in next year's midterms and potentially benefit Democrats.\par \par \uc2 "The energy and the single-issue fervor has usually occurred among pro-life women,'' said Christine Matthews, a pollster who has worked for Republican candidates. But the prospect of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions could serve as a wakeup call for women who favor \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and now see them as under threat, she said.\par \par \uc2 "In some of these suburban areas, if they were thinking of voting for a potential Republican for governor because he or she seemed good on the economy, this could now be a deciding factor not to,'' she said.\par \par \uc2 Democrats also pointed to the provision in the Texas law allowing private parties to file lawsuits against any person who allegedly performs or aids a banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saying that would serve to drive voters.\par \par \uc2 In NBC News polling in August, 54% of adults said \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be legal in all or most cases. But support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights was particularly high among younger voters, those ages 18 to 34. Some 65% of that group supported \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights in most cases, 33 points higher than opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Opposition to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights was high among evangelical Christians in they survey, with 70% saying \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be illegal in all or most cases.\par \par \uc2 Some Republicans say anti-\b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  voters are being underestimated.\par \par \uc2 "You will see that the social conservative wing of the Republican party and the pro-life advocates engage like you couldn't believe on this issue," said Alice Stewart, a Republican strategist who worked on Sen. Ted Cruz's 2016 presidential campaign.\par \par \uc2 Most Democrats are united around the issue of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Former Illinois Rep. Dan Lipinksi, one of the few Democrats who opposed apportion rights, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/marie-newman-defeats-rep-dan-lipinski-in-illinois-primary-challenge-11584507001"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 lost his seat in a primary }}}\uc2  last year centered around the topic.\par \par \uc2 In the Senate, 48 of the 50 Democratic senators are cosponsors of the Senate version of the Women's Health Protection Act. Sens. Joe Manchin (D., W. Va.) and Bob Casey (D., Pa.) haven't signed on. Mr. Manchin's and Mr. Casey's offices didn't immediately respond to requests for comment.\par \par \uc2 No Republicans are cosponsors, though Sens. \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  of Maine and Lisa Murkowski of Alaska have said they support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In a statement, Ms. Collins criticized the court's decision to allow the law, which she called "extreme and harmful" to remain in effect. A representative for Ms. Murkowski didn't immediately respond to a request for information on their plans.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said Thursday that Mr. Biden would support efforts to codify \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  protections by Congress.\par \par \uc2 Aside from legislation, some progressive Democrats have also called for expanding the number of justices on the Supreme Court, to counteract the current 6-3 conservative majority, or to introduce term limits for justices. In April, Mr. Biden ordered a commission to study changes such as adding seats, and the White House said that effort is continuing.\par \par \uc2 Rep. Jerrold Nadler\uc2  (D., N.Y.) , the chair of the House Judiciary Committee, also announced Thursday his committee would hold hearings on the court's decision.\par \par \uc2 Write to Eliza Collins at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:eliza.collins+1@wsj.com."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 eliza.collins+1@wsj.com. }}}\uc2  and Aaron Zitner at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:aaron.zitner@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 aaron.zitner@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/abortion-rights-house-vote-planned-by-pelosi-after-supreme-court-decision-11630603877"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Pelosi Plans \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Rights Vote for House After Supreme Court's Texas Decision }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210902eh920040h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
