\par\par \uc2 Business\par \uc2 Business\par \b \uc2 After Texas  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law, Match CEO, Bumble Create Funds to Support Those Affected; Leaders of Texas-based dating apps call new restrictions 'regressive'; governor says business not turned off by state's policies\b0\par\par\uc2 By Talal Ansari \par \uc2 596 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2021\par 21:20 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Leaders at two of the most popular dating apps in the U.S. are creating funds to aid Texas workers and their families affected by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-what-to-know-as-supreme-court-allows-it-to-take-effect-11630606238"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the state's new \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The law, which went into effect Wednesday, bars the procedure after about six weeks of pregnancy. The Supreme Court, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-emergency-request-to-block-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630556283"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in a 5-4 vote }}}\uc2  late Wednesday, declined to block what is now the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-takes-effect-pending-supreme-court-action-11630498466"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 nation's toughest restrictions on abortions }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Match Group Inc\uc2 . Chief Executive \uc2 Shar Dubey\uc2  told her staff in a memo that she plans to set up a fund to assist Texas-based employees or their dependents who will now need to seek care out of the state.\par \par \uc2 Ms. Dubey said that while the Dallas-based company usually doesn't take political stands unless it relates to its business, she felt compelled to speak out as a woman in Texas.\par \par \uc2 "I'm speaking about this personally, as a mother and a woman who has fervently cared about women's rights, including the very fundamental right of choice over her body\u8212\'20\'14this is a very sad day," she said, calling the state's laws "more regressive than most of the world," including India, where she emigrated from.\par \par \uc2 When \uc2 Texas Gov. Greg Abbott{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-ban-11621452346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 signed the legislation }}}\uc2  in May, the Republican said it "ensures that the life of every unborn child who has a heartbeat will be saved from the ravages of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Austin-based \uc2 Bumble Inc\uc2 ., which operates another popular dating app, said Wednesday it was setting up a similar fund for its workers. "Bumble is women-founded and women-led, and from day one we've stood up for the most vulnerable. We'll keep fighting against regressive laws like #SB8," the company {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/bumble/status/1433194713092403202?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said in a tweet }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Texas Heartbeat Act, also known as SB 8, passed into law earlier this year by the Republican-controlled legislature. It says a physician can't knowingly perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there is "a detectable fetal heartbeat." In practice, this restricts most abortions after about six weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The law, which allows private citizens to file civil lawsuits to enforce the restrictions, left clinic directors, doctors and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-new-texas-abortion-ban-law-takes-effect-providers-rush-to-adjust-11630521388"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 adapting to the new measures }}}\uc2  Wednesday. Clinics were inundated with calls as patients sought guidance, and many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in the state were squeezing in patients and performing procedures until minutes before midnight, when the law took effect, according to clinic leaders.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Abbott, in a CNBC interview on Thursday, said business wasn't turned off by Texas's policies. He said Tesla Inc. Chief Executive \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 , who has growing businesses in Texas, had told him he liked the social policies in the state.\par \par \uc2 After the governor's comments, Mr. Musk {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/elonmusk/status/1433474893316722691?s=20"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted }}}\uc2  "I would prefer to stay out of politics." He also said in the tweet that he believed "government should rarely impose its will upon the people."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Musk last year said he moved to Texas from California and, at the time, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/elon-musk-to-discuss-teslas-banner-year-despite-pandemic-silicon-valleys-future-11607449988"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 took aim at Silicon Valley }}}\uc2 , arguing it had too much influence. Tesla is building a car plant near Austin and the billionaire's rocket venture, known as \uc2 SpaceX\uc2 , also has a facility in the state. Both companies also maintain large operations in California.\par \par \uc2 Write to Talal Ansari at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:talal.ansari@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 talal.ansari@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/after-texas-abortion-law-match-ceo-bumble-create-funds-to-support-those-affected-11630617641"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 After Texas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law, Match CEO, Bumble Create Funds to Support Those Affected }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210902eh92006bt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
