\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Texas  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law Takes Effect Pending Supreme Court Action; Justices haven't acted on request by  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  providers to block the state's so-called fetal-heartbeat law\b0\par\par\uc2 By Brent Kendall,Jess Bravin and Jacob Gershman \par \uc2 1,161 \uc2 words\par \uc2 1 September 2021\par 23:36 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections\par \par \uc2 An earlier version of this article incorrectly gave the name of Texas clinic operator Whole Woman's Health as Whole Women's Health and the name of Live Action, a group that opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, as Life Action. (Corrected on Sept. 1 and 2)\par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14A new Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law that bars the procedure after about six weeks of pregnancy took effect Wednesday, after the Supreme Court didn't act on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-asked-to-intervene-on-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630355606"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 an emergency request }}}\uc2  by clinics and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates to block it.\par \par \uc2 When the court said nothing Tuesday by midnight, the ban officially went into force, making it the most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law in effect in the U.S. The high court still could choose to act soon.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-ban-11621452346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The state law }}}\uc2 , signed by Republican Gov. Greg Abbott in May with an effective date of Sept. 1, dictates that a physician can't knowingly perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there is "a detectable fetal heartbeat," which includes embryonic cardiac activity that appears about six weeks into a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 A ban on abortions occurring at such an early stage of pregnancy\u8212\'20\'14before some women realize they are pregnant\u8212\'20\'14conflicts with current Supreme Court precedent. The high court has previously forbidden states from banning the procedure {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mississippi-asks-supreme-court-to-end-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-11626985810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 before a fetus is able to live outside the womb }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The matter, which only arrived at the Supreme Court on Monday, is centered on the preliminary question of what rules should apply in Texas while \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/judge-imposes-new-limits-on-texas-abortion-ban-during-coronavirus-crisis-11586481818"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 continue to challenge the ban }}}\uc2  in lower courts. That issue came to the justices after a federal appeals court halted trial-court proceedings in the case for now and declined to block the ban from taking effect.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers in Texas were squeezing in patients and performing procedures until minutes before midnight when restrictions took effect, said Amy Hagstrom Miller, the founder and chief executive of Whole Woman's Health, which operates clinics in Texas and has previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-voids-texas-abortion-regulations-1467036610"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 challenged Texas \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions }}}\uc2  before the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 All four Whole Woman's Health clinics in Texas were open Wednesday and operating in accordance with the new law, Ms. Miller said. The clinics are able to offer ultrasounds and make plans to provide the procedure for anyone without detectable embryonic activity.\par \par \uc2 Houston Women's Reproductive Services is no longer providing abortions past the six-week mark, in accordance to the law, said Kathy Kleinfeld, the clinic's administrator.\par \par \uc2 "There's confusion, frustration, desperation," she said.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents said Wednesday's developments were historic.\par \par \uc2 "Right now in the great state of Texas, every single child with a detectable heartbeat is legally protected from being killed by the violence of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Lila Rose, founder and president of Live Action, an antiabortion-rights group. "This is a historic step forward for basic human rights, but more progress must be made."\par \par \uc2 Others remained cautious about claiming a victory before action by the Supreme Court, which some anticipated coming on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 "We're definitely optimistic that this is a good sign," said John Seago, legislative director of Texas Right to Life. "We're not fully celebrating until we see an official ruling later today."\par \par \uc2 State lawmakers designed the ban in a way that makes it more difficult for litigants to challenge in court.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates typically challenge new restrictions before they go into effect by suing the government officials who would be in charge of enforcing the law. But Texas lawmakers devised a measure that shifts enforcement from the state to private parties. Under the terms of the six-week ban, private parties can file civil lawsuits against any person who allegedly performs or aids a banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or who intends to do so. Under the law, a successful suit entitles the plaintiff to collect at least $10,000 in damages per \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  challenged.\par \par \uc2 State officials emphasized this feature of the law in papers filed Tuesday afternoon with the Supreme Court, arguing it was among many reasons \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers weren't entitled to an emergency order blocking the law.\par \par \uc2 "This court cannot expunge the law itself. Rather, it can enjoin only enforcement of the law. But the governmental defendants explicitly don't enforce the law," Texas Republican Attorney General \uc2 Ken Paxton\uc2  and other state officials told the high court.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics challenging the law put it differently. The measure replaces established legal procedures "with distorted versions designed to maximize the abusive and harassing nature of the lawsuits and to make them impossible to fairly defend against," they said in their Supreme Court filing.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Seago said Texas Right to Life isn't currently planning to bring enforcement lawsuits and is working under the assumption that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers are complying with the law for now.\par \par \uc2 Roughly a dozen states have passed so-called heartbeat bills but none of the other measures are in effect, and they differ from Texas's private-enforcement approach. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters say the fetal-heartbeat terminology used to describe the six-week bans is misleading because an embryo isn't deemed a fetus until the 11th week of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 An \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic or doctor still can challenge the constitutionality of the law if and when they get sued, but \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters say that approach could put the provider in financial jeopardy. Having the law in effect will "immediately and irreparably decimate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Texas," the providers said in their brief.\par \par \uc2 President Biden weighed in Wednesday, saying the Texas law "blatantly violates the constitutional right established under Roe v. Wade and upheld as precedent for nearly half a century."\par \par \uc2 Though the Texas law is in effect for now, separate state-court litigation could reduce some of its immediate impact.\par \par \uc2 Earlier Tuesday, Travis County District Court Judge Amy Clark Meachum, a Democrat elected to the bench, temporarily barred a statewide antiabortion group from bringing enforcement lawsuits against several plaintiffs who are challenging the new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban in her court.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs include a Plano, Texas, attorney who has donated to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights causes and a Dallas attorney who represents women impregnated by sexual assault. In court filings, they said they feared that giving money to groups that support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access or providing legal counsel to assault victims considering abortions could subject them to suits under the law.\par \par \uc2 Texas Right to Life, a defendant in the Travis County lawsuits, said it never threatened to sue those specific plaintiffs.\par \par \uc2 Judge Meachum has scheduled a Sept. 13 court hearing on whether to bar such lawsuits for a longer period.\par \par \uc2 Jennifer Calfas and Sarah Toy contributed to this article.\par \par \uc2 Write to Brent Kendall at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:brent.kendall@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brent.kendall@wsj.com }}}\uc2 , Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jess.bravin+1@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jess.bravin+1@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Jacob Gershman at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jacob.gershman@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jacob.gershman@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-abortion-law-takes-effect-pending-supreme-court-action-11630498466"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law Takes Effect Pending Supreme Court Action  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210901eh910018h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
