\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court Asked to Intervene on Texas Six-Week  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; State's so-called fetal-heartbeat law is set to go into effect this week\b0\par\par\uc2 By Brent Kendall \par \uc2 636 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 August 2021\par 21:55 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14\b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers filed an emergency request with the Supreme Court on Monday seeking to prevent a Texas law that bans the procedure after approximately six weeks of pregnancy from going into effect.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-ban-11621452346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The state law }}}\uc2 , signed by Texas Republican Gov. Greg Abbott in May, says a physician can't knowingly perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  if there is a detectable fetal heartbeat, which the law defines to include cardiac activity in the embryo that appears about six weeks into a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The law, set to take effect on Sept. 1, has an unusual feature that could complicate court proceedings. Texas lawmakers barred state officials from directly enforcing the measure, effectively deputizing the public to do it instead. The Texas law allows for private civil lawsuits in which members of the public can sue\u8212\'20\'14and collect at least $10,000 in damages\u8212\'20\'14from any person who allegedly performs or aids a banned \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or who intends to do so.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights supporters say state lawmakers designed the measure this way to make it more difficult to bring a court challenge against a ban that would be unconstitutional under current Supreme Court precedent.\par \par \uc2 In a bid to invalidate the ban, a group of providers and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates in July sued several state officials and a private citizen who had expressed interest in bringing litigation to enforce the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law. The Fifth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals, without detailed explanation, has halted trial-court proceedings in the case for now and declined to block the ban from going into effect.\par \par \uc2 The plaintiffs on Monday filed an emergency application at the Supreme Court that asks for the ban to be put on hold while litigation continues.\par \par \uc2 If the law goes into effect, the plaintiffs said in their high-court filing, it "would immediately and irreparably decimate \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access in Texas, barring care for at least 85% of Texas \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  patients (those who are six weeks pregnant or greater) and likely forcing many \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics to ultimately close."\par \par \uc2 Many women don't even know they are pregnant at six weeks, they said.\par \par \uc2 The fast-moving dispute comes ahead of a major \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  case set for the Supreme Court's coming term. In that litigation, the court will be deciding on the legality of a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-consider-abortion-restrictions-from-mississippi-11621259099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law }}}\uc2  that aims to ban the procedure after 15 weeks of pregnancy, a case that gives the justices an opportunity to revisit precedents protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. A decision in that case is expected by next June.\par \par \uc2 Supreme Court precedents have allowed states to regulate, but not outright ban, \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the pre-viability months of pregnancy. Conservative lawmakers have stepped up efforts to test those precedents since the 2018 retirement of Justice \uc2 Anthony Kennedy\uc2 , a maverick conservative who was the court's longtime pivotal vote protecting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 When he signed the legislation in May, Mr. Abbott said it "ensures that the life of every unborn child who has a heartbeat will be saved from the ravages of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The Texas litigation is the latest in a series of emergency appeals that have landed at the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-supreme-courts-shadow-docket-how-it-works-11629901875"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 during the justices' summer break }}}\uc2 . The court this month already has lifted a federal public-health {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-blocks-new-eviction-moratorium-11630028819"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ban on evictions }}}\uc2 , loosened {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-lifts-part-of-new-yorks-eviction-moratorium-11628818541"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 New York's eviction moratorium }}}\uc2 , cleared \uc2 Indiana University\uc2  to proceed with a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-rejects-request-to-block-indiana-universitys-vaccine-mandate-for-students-11628809855"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Covid-19 vaccine mandate }}}\uc2  for the fall semester and reinstated a Trump-era policy that requires asylum seekers at the southern U.S. border {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-reinstates-remain-in-mexico-policy-for-asylum-applicants-11629849547"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to wait in Mexico }}}\uc2  while their claims are evaluated.\par \par \uc2 Write to Brent Kendall at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:brent.kendall@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brent.kendall@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-asked-to-intervene-on-texas-six-week-abortion-ban-11630355606"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court Asked to Intervene on Texas Six-Week \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210830eh8u003xp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
