\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Mississippi Asks Supreme Court to End Roe v. Wade  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Rights; State's brief for coming high court case says landmark  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  decision violates Constitution's provisions on states' rights\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jess Bravin \par \uc2 883 \uc2 words\par \uc2 22 July 2021\par 22:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Mississippi asked the Supreme Court Thursday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to abolish federal \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights }}}\uc2 , arguing in a brief that Roe v. Wade and other precedents entitling women to end their pregnancies in some circumstances trample on states' 10th-Amendment powers to decide public policy within their borders.\par \par \uc2 In May, the Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-consider-abortion-restrictions-from-mississippi-11621259099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreed to hear Mississippi's appeal }}}\uc2  of a 2019 appeals court decision striking down a state law prohibiting abortions after the 15th week of pregnancy. The case, Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization, is to be argued after the court's new term begins in October, with a decision expected by next summer.\par \par \uc2 The Mississippi case has been regarded as a bellwether for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, challenging precedents that set viability\u8212\'20\'14the fetus's ability to survive outside the womb\u8212\'20\'14as the baseline for expanded government power to restrict the procedure. In its initial appeal, filed in June 2020, Mississippi argued its Gestational Age Act complied with existing precedent, suggesting that Roe be overruled only if the court found no other way to uphold the state law.\par \par \uc2 But {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization--Brief for Petitioners (final) (1).pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the brief filed Thursday }}}\uc2  reframed the arguments, taking direct aim at the 1973 Roe decision and a 1992 follow-up, Planned Parenthood v. Casey, that narrowed Roe's scope. Under current precedent, regulations that place an undue burden on women seeking \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  are unconstitutional.\par \par \uc2 "Roe and Casey are egregiously wrong. The conclusion that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a constitutional right has no basis in text, structure, history, or tradition," Mississippi argued. "Roe broke from prior cases, Casey failed to rehabilitate it, and both recognize a right that has no basis in the Constitution."\par \par \uc2 Read Mississippi's argument in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization--Brief for Petitioners (final) (1).pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization }}}\par \par \uc2 Even if there were policy reasons to allow women the right to end pregnancy in 1973, the state argued that times had changed.\par \par \uc2 "The march of progress has left Roe and Casey behind," Mississippi said in the brief. "Those cases maintained that an unwanted pregnancy could doom women to 'a distressful life and future,' that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a needed complement to contraception, and that viability marked a sensible point for when state interests in unborn life become compelling."\par \par \uc2 But "today, adoption is accessible and on a wide scale women attain both professional success and a rich family life, contraceptives are more available and effective, and scientific advances show that an unborn child has taken on the human form and features months before viability," the state argues.\par \par \uc2 "If Roe falls, half the states in the country are poised to ban \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  entirely," said \uc2 Nancy Northup\uc2 , president of the Center for \b \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which represents the Jackson Women's Health Organization in the case. "Women of childbearing age in the U.S. have never known a world in which they don't have this basic right, and we will keep fighting to make sure they never will," she said.\par \par \uc2 When Mississippi filed its initial appeal in June 2020, the court's direction hung on the vote of Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2 , who has been skeptical of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights but, in recent cases, reluctant to discard wholesale the precedents recognizing them. With the court otherwise divided between other conservatives hostile to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and four liberals committed to their defense, antiabortion activists typically {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-strikes-down-louisiana-abortion-law-11593440418"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 framed litigation to chip away at precedents }}}\uc2  rather than overruling them.\par \par \uc2 The {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ruth-bader-ginsburg-dies-11600472623"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 September death }}}\uc2  of Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  changed the calculus, allowing then President \uc2 Donald Trump{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/amy-coney-barrett-set-to-be-confirmed-as-supreme-court-justice-11603721947"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to appoint }}}\uc2  Justice Amy Coney Barrett, who in private life had belonged to an antiabortion organization. As is typical for judicial nominees, Judge Barrett {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/politics-dominates-as-amy-coney-barretts-confirmation-hearings-begin-in-senate-11602495000?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said during her confirmation hearing that her personal views wouldn't influence her approach }}}\uc2  to deciding cases.\par \par \uc2 During a 2016 campaign debate, Mr. Trump said were he given three Supreme Court appointments, Roe would be overruled "automatically." With Justice Barrett joining Justices \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  and \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 , the Mississippi case now is poised to test Mr. Trump's prediction. Two other justices, \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  and \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2 , have consistently voted against \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 In March Mississippi Attorney General Lynn Fitch, a Republican, hired Scott Stewart, a veteran of the Trump Justice Department and former law clerk to Justice Thomas, as state solicitor general. Mr. Stewart is expected to argue the case.\par \par \uc2 The opposing brief from the Jackson Women's Health Organization, the state's only \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic, is due Sept. 13. In an initial brief filed last August, the clinic argued that 50 years of precedent had established viability as a clear marker where the balance between a woman's rights over her body begin to yield to a state's interest in protecting potential life.\par \par \uc2 "Before viability, the State's interests, whatever they may be, cannot override a pregnant person's interests in their liberty and autonomy over their own body," the clinic argued.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Do you think the current members of the Supreme Court are likely to significantly curtail a woman's ability to get an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jess.bravin+1@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jess.bravin+1@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/mississippi-asks-supreme-court-to-end-roe-v-wade-abortion-rights-11626985810"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mississippi Asks Supreme Court to End Roe v. Wade \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Rights }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210722eh7m005mt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
