\par\par \uc2 Washington Wire\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Groups on Both Sides of  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Debate Prepare for 2022 Battle; Susan B. Anthony List plans campaign aimed at blunting President Biden's ability to appoint judges\b0\par\par\uc2 By Gabriel T. Rubin \par \uc2 933 \uc2 words\par \uc2 16 July 2021\par 09:30 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ANTIABORTION GROUP SUSAN B. ANTHONY LIST plans to mount a $73 million campaign in the 2022 midterms to topple Democratic congressional majorities, especially in the Senate to blunt President Biden's {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-has-first-shot-at-judicial-vacancies-11617012000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ability to appoint judges  }}}\uc2 . The group spent $61.5 million to re-elect former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and a Republican Senate in 2020. It sees a decadeslong effort to install an antiabortion judiciary and build power at the state level nearing its pinnacle with {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-aims-to-appoint-liberal-judges-after-trumps-conservative-push-11606559402"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 6-3 conservative Supreme Court advantage  }}}\uc2  and a slew of challenges to Roe v.\par \par \uc2 Wade coming through {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/states-are-shifting-farther-apart-on-abortion-11549656745"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the litigation pipeline  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We've always put all our eggs in the Senate basket," said Mallory Quigley, the SBA List's vice president of communications. "We relish the opportunity to talk about what the court means for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-consider-abortion-restrictions-from-mississippi-11621259099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 will hear a case on Mississippi's legislation  }}}\uc2  to prohibit abortions after 15 weeks in the coming term, and likely reach a decision next June or early July, four months before the election. SBA List plans to blanket the airwaves around the decision and deploy local canvassers to knock on doors in competitive states and districts. The first group of canvassers began training this week, in Arizona and Georgia, Republicans' top two 2022 target seats.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How important do you think \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be as an issue in the 2022 midterm elections? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 , on the other side of the issue, has also already begun its effort to defend the Democratic Senate majority. In recent weeks the organization's New Hampshire affiliate has been running digital ads against Gov. \uc2 Chris Sununu\uc2  , the top Republican choice to run against Sen. \uc2 Maggie Hassan\uc2  , though {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/hassan-stresses-independence-as-she-faces-2022-election-threat-11619172000"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 he has not said definitively whether he'll run  }}}\uc2 . He recently signed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.concordmonitor.com/2022-election-ad-wars-already-underway-41377933"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a budget that enacts new \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  restrictions  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2 's political arm is primarily focused on the 2021 gubernatorial and state legislative races in Virginia and New Jersey, a spokesman said, and has not yet finalized its 2022 budget. "Voters in 2021 and 2022 will continue to reject candidates bent on attacking their \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  and access to essential healthcare," said Jenny Lawson, executive director of \uc2 Planned Parenthood\uc2  Votes.\par \par \uc2 HEARING-AID COMPANIES could face a new reality of lower prices and more competition if the regulators act quickly on a Biden order to open up the market for nonprescription devices. The four companies that control around 85% of the hearing-aid industry have been in limbo since 2017, when Congress mandated the Food and Drug Administration to come up with rules for over-the-counter hearing aids, which would lower prices for many devices. An estimated 48 million people in the U.S. have hearing loss, though only around 14% use hearing aids. Currently, many devices require a visit to a specialist, aren't covered by insurance, and can cost several thousand dollars. The Hearing Industries Association {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://betterhearing.org/newsroom/blogs/while-we-wait-for-over-the-counter-hearing-aids/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 says it wants to keep those specialist consultations  }}}\uc2 so customers can "make an informed decision about whether the OTC hearing aids will provide benefit."\par \par \uc2 Congress's 2017 action was the opening salvo of a long fight. The \uc2 FDA\uc2  missed a 2020 deadline, frustrating the legislation's backers. But now firms are grappling with the new reality: a spokesman for hearing-aid heavyweight \uc2 Sonova\uc2  said they were "assessing all options\u8230\'20\'26to determine if and how to participate in this emerging OTC segment." But change comes slowly: The final rule could "come into effect in mid-to-late 2022 at the earliest," he added.\par \par \uc2 CHAD WOLF\uc2  , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-names-chad-wolf-to-be-acting-homeland-security-secretary-11572646900"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Trump-era acting leader of the Department of Homeland Security  }}}\uc2 , has recently been approached about running for congressional office, people familiar with the matter say. Congressional lawmakers and other Republicans have approached Wolf in recent weeks about whether he would consider running for office in Texas, his previous home state.\par \par \uc2 While Wolf hasn't made up his mind yet, people who know him say he has considered running for office for years. Since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/chad-wolf-steps-down-as-acting-secretary-of-homeland-security-11610403841"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 stepping down from DHS earlier this year  }}}\uc2 , Wolf has stayed in the fray, becoming chairman of a center focused on immigration and homeland security at the \uc2 America First Policy Institute\uc2 , a think tank set up by Trump allies. He also spoke at the Conservative Political Action Conference earlier this month on a panel titled "Can Cancel Culture Be Canceled?"\par \par \uc2 MIKE PENCE is delivering a series of policy speeches as he aims to re-emerge as his own political figure after leaving the vice presidency. On Wednesday, he spoke at \uc2 the Heritage Foundation\uc2  about competition with China, and he has plans to speak about law enforcement, "liberal excess and overreach in our education system," and another foreign-policy speech over the next year, according to a person familiar with his plans. Last month, he spoke in New Hampshire, where he acknowledged that he and Trump "may never see eye-to-eye" on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/at-the-u-s-capitol-a-milling-crowd-sparked-a-riot-in-a-few-crucial-minutes-11610067766"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the Capitol riot  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 MINOR MEMOS: Enthusiastic Arizona election audit volunteer does "YMCA" dance while counting ballots in GOP-ordered recount\u8230\'20\'26Former Iowa Sen. Tom Harkin interrupts radio interview to shoo deer away from his wife's garden\u8230\'20\'26Harkin's successor in the Senate, Sen. \uc2 Joni Ernst\uc2  , debuts "The Price is Right" spinning wheel on the Senate floor, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/cspan/status/1415377736911233027"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 re-christened "The Price is Up"  }}}\uc2  to knock Democrats for rising inflation.\par \par \uc2 Write to Gabriel T. Rubin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:gabriel.rubin@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 gabriel.rubin@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/groups-on-both-sides-of-abortion-debate-prepare-for-2022-battle-11626427801"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Groups on Both Sides of \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Debate Prepare for 2022 Battle  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210716eh7g000rz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
