\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Missouri's Down-Syndrome  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law Blocked; Federal appeals court says the state may not enforce a law limiting abortions sought solely because of a Down syndrome diagnosis\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jacob Gershman \par \uc2 692 \uc2 words\par \uc2 9 June 2021\par 21:31 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 A divided federal appeals court Wednesday blocked Missouri from enforcing a law limiting abortions for women who want to terminate a fetus for fear that it has Down syndrome.\par \par \uc2 The three-judge panel also blocked other provisions of the law that banned most abortions after eight weeks gestational age.\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led Legislature passed the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://house.mo.gov/bill.aspx?bill=HB126&year=2019&code=R"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 "Missouri Stands for the Unborn Act" }}}\uc2  in 2019, among a wave of similar \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions enacted by conservative-leaning states in recent years.\par \par \uc2 The Missouri law makes it illegal for a physician to perform an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  upon learning that the patient wants the procedure solely because she fears the fetus has Down syndrome.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2  and \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  of Missouri filed suit challenging the law as unconstitutional, representing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinics in the St. Louis area.\par \par \uc2 A federal judge in 2019 blocked the Down syndrome rule and the broader \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  ban, though it left in place restrictions on abortions because of the fetus's sex or race.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://ecf.ca8.uscourts.gov/opndir/21/06/192882P.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 In Wednesday's decision }}}\uc2 , the St. Louis-based Eighth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals panel agreed with the lower court. In a 2-1 piece of the decision, the court said the part of the law protecting fetuses with the genetic disorder was a "closer call" but concluded that it threatened to violate at least some women's constitutional rights to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In a unanimous part of the decision, the court cited longstanding Supreme Court precedent barring states from restricting abortions before the point at which the fetus has reached the stage of viability.\par \par \uc2 "[W]hile the Down Syndrome Provision might impact fewer people than the Gestational Age Provisions, the nature of the harm\u8212\'20\'14the inability to obtain an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability\u8212\'20\'14is at least equally significant," wrote Circuit Judge Jane L. Kelly, a President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  appointee, in the opinion.\par \par \uc2 In a dissenting opinion, Circuit Judge David R. Stras, a President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointee, said he would uphold the Down syndrome provision, stating that plaintiffs never showed that the rule would actually prevent women from getting abortions.\par \par \uc2 In response, the regional Planned Parenthood called the ruling a "critical victory" for Missouri residents.\par \par \uc2 "For now, we celebrate our continued ability to provide safe, legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the last remaining clinic in Missouri," the head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights organization, Yamelsie Rodr\u237\'00\'EDguez, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/PPSLR/status/1402652224657014790"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 tweeted }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Republican Missouri Attorney General Eric S. Schmitt said he plans to ask the Supreme Court to review the decision.\par \par \uc2 "While we're disappointed in the Eighth Circuit's decision, their decision does provide an avenue for this case to be heard by the Supreme Court, and we plan to seek review," he stated.\par \par \uc2 In its briefs, the attorney general's office wrote that the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  of children with Down syndrome is approaching "genocidal levels."\par \par \uc2 Federal appeals courts have consistently struck down \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  bans at such early stages of pregnancy. But appellate courts have disagreed over whether states can put restraints on abortions performed because of predicted characteristics of the fetus.\par \par \uc2 In April, the Sixth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals in Cincinnati {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/federal-appeals-court-upholds-ohios-down-syndrome-abortion-law-11618348943"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 voted 9-7 }}}\uc2  to uphold an Ohio law that similarly limited abortions targeting Down syndrome, disagreeing with other circuit court rulings on the issue.\par \par \uc2 Around a dozen states have active laws on the books restricting abortions based on one or more fetal characteristics: the sex or race of the fetus or because of a genetic anomaly, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.guttmacher.org/state-policy/explore/abortion-bans-cases-sex-or-race-selection-or-genetic-anomaly"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 according to the Guttmacher Institute }}}\uc2 , a research group that promotes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. Most of the laws restricting abortions based on genetic anomaly aren't currently enforced, according to the institute.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court has never reviewed the constitutionality of such restraints.\par \par \uc2 The Missouri ruling comes in the wake of the Supreme Court's decision last month {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-consider-abortion-restrictions-from-mississippi-11621259099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to hear a challenge to a Mississippi law }}}\uc2  that bans abortions after about 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jacob Gershman at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jacob.gershman@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jacob.gershman@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/missouris-down-syndrome-abortion-law-blocked-11623274315"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Missouri's Down-Syndrome \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law Blocked  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210609eh69006hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
