\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Biden Budget Plan Would Remove Ban on Federal Funds for  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 ; The 1976 Hyde Amendment, included in spending legislation for decades, is backed by most Republicans\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 595 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 May 2021\par 20:40 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 President Biden's budget proposal removes language banning the use of federal dollars for abortions in most cases, fulfilling a campaign pledge and setting up a fight in Congress, where most Republicans are opposed to the change.\par \par \uc2 The president's budget, released Friday, doesn't include the 1976 Hyde Amendment, which bars federal funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with exceptions for victims of rape or incest or if the mother's life is in danger. The language has been included in spending legislation for decades, and Mr. Biden had supported the amendment for years before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-reverses-stance-on-hyde-amendment-citing-roe-v-wade-11559871101?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversing his position during his presidential campaign }}}\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates and many Democrats had urged him to do so.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents say the amendment ensures federal tax dollars don't go to paying for the procedure, while advocates for access to abortions say it disproportionately affects low-income women and women of color who are Medicaid recipients.\par \par \uc2 The decision from the president comes as some Republican-led {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-ban-11621452346?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states add new restrictions }}}\uc2 on abortions and the Supreme Court prepares to consider {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-consider-abortion-restrictions-from-mississippi-11621259099?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the legality of a Mississippi \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law }}}\uc2  that sought to ban the procedure after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 While this marked the first time in decades that a president sought to strip the language, the change wasn't highlighted in a budget fact sheet released by the White House. Some \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates have pushed for Mr. Biden to be more vocal on the issue, noting that he didn't use the word \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a statement marking the anniversary of Roe v. Wade, the 1973 Supreme Court decision recognizing a woman's right to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , or in his recent address to a joint session of Congress.\par \par \uc2 "We are thrilled that President Biden followed through on his campaign promise and kept the Hyde Amendment out of his budget," said Destiny Lopez, co-president of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocacy group All* Above All. "We urge Biden to now use his bully pulpit to stop the bullying of the Hyde Amendment and offer full-throated support for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  justice."\par \par \uc2 Marjorie Dannenfelser, president of the antiabortion \uc2 Susan B. Anthony\uc2  List, said that Mr. Biden's budget threw "longstanding, bipartisan consensus out the window to fulfill a campaign promise to the radical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby."\par \par \uc2 Democrats currently have a narrow hold on the House, where spending bills can pass with a simple majority. But in the Senate, split 50-50, most legislation must win 60 votes, making the elimination of the Hyde Amendment a tall order. A total of 200 House Republicans and 48 Senate Republicans have signed letters saying they will oppose any spending bills that don't include the Hyde Amendment.\par \par \uc2 Sen. Patty Murray\uc2  (D., Wash.) said that she was working to build support in the Senate for eliminating the Hyde Amendment.\par \par \uc2 Republican Study Committee Chairman Jim Banks (R., Ind.), who organized the House letter, called the president's budget reckless and criticized Mr. Biden for not including the Hyde Amendment.\par \par \uc2 Polls show {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/record-71-of-voters-oppose-overturning-roe-v-wade-1532379600?mod=article_inline"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most Americans say \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  should be legal }}}\uc2 , but support is much higher among Democrats than Republicans. Overall support has grown in recent years. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights organizations are a key Democratic constituency and a link to women in the party\u8212\'20\'14voters who could play a key role in the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-budget-plan-would-remove-ban-on-federal-funds-for-abortion-11622231319"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden Budget Plan Would Remove Ban on Federal Funds for \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210528eh5s005sd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
