\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Biden's Budget to Spotlight Battle Over  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Restrictions; President said during his campaign that he backed scrapping a ban on federal dollars for abortions in most cases, known as the Hyde Amendment\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey \par \uc2 1,093 \uc2 words\par \uc2 27 May 2021\par 12:34 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 President Biden's coming budget proposal will include his decision on whether to push to end a ban on using federal dollars for abortions in most cases, potentially opening a new front in the clash over access to the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden said during his presidential campaign that he {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-reverses-stance-on-hyde-amendment-citing-roe-v-wade-11559871101"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 backed scrapping the ban }}}\uc2 , known as the Hyde Amendment, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bidens-views-on-abortion-draw-fresh-criticism-and-expose-rift-with-fellow-democrats-11559766838"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversing his longstanding position }}}\uc2  in favor of the measure that has been included in spending bills for decades.\par \par \uc2 Keeping the language out of his Friday budget proposal would be welcomed by many Democrats and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates, but eliminating the Hyde Amendment would face headwinds in Congress, where most Republicans are opposed.\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 Should the Hyde Amendment be removed from congressional appropriations bills? Why or why not? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden's budget proposal won't likely be enacted in full by lawmakers, but it serves as a statement of the White House's priorities. And his decision comes as some {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-ban-11621452346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states add new restrictions }}}\uc2  on abortions and the Supreme Court prepares to consider {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-consider-abortion-restrictions-from-mississippi-11621259099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the legality of a Mississippi \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  law }}}\uc2  that sought to ban the procedure after 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The White House declined to discuss the budget but said the president's position on the Hyde Amendment hasn't changed since his campaign statements.\par \par \uc2 Melanie Newman, senior vice president of communications and culture for the Planned Parenthood Federation of America, said in a memo released Tuesday that removing the amendment from the budget "would send a clear signal from the president of the United States that our federal laws should support everyone's ability to access comprehensive healthcare services, including safe, legal \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Democrats currently have a narrow hold on the House, where spending bills can pass with a simple majority. But in the Senate, split 50-50, most legislation must win 60 votes, making the elimination of the Hyde Amendment a tall order.\par \par \uc2 A total of 200 House Republicans and 48 Senate Republicans have signed letters saying they will oppose any spending bills that don't include the Hyde Amendment, which they say ensures federal tax dollars don't go to paying for abortions.\par \par \uc2 "It's my hope that we'll push back hard enough that [House Speaker Nancy] Pelosi and [Senate Majority Leader Chuck] Schumer and Biden will think twice and do the right thing and protect taxpayers from funding abortions," said Republican Study Committee Chairman Jim Banks (R., Ind.), who organized the House letter.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates say the 1976 Hyde Amendment disproportionately affects low-income women and women of color who are Medicaid recipients because the program doesn't pay for abortions with federal funds except in limited circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Should he strip the amendment from the budget proposal, Mr. Biden would be the first president to do so since President \uc2 Bill Clinton\uc2  in 1993. President \uc2 Barack Obama\uc2  included it in his budget proposals, and for decades Democrats have included the amendment in legislation that required bipartisan support. The party included opposition to the Hyde Amendment in the party platform for the first time in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Polls show {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/record-71-of-voters-oppose-overturning-roe-v-wade-1532379600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most Americans say \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  should be legal }}}\uc2 , but support is much higher among Democrats than Republicans. Overall support has grown in recent years. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights organizations are a key Democratic constituency and a connection to women in the party\u8212\'20\'14voters who could play a key role in the midterm elections.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden, who is Roman Catholic, noted in his 2007 book, "Promises to Keep," that he had maintained a "middle of the road position on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," opposing efforts to curtail a woman's right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including a constitutional amendment to overturn Roe v. Wade, but voting against late-term \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and federal funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  services.\par \par \uc2 Since taking office, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-reverse-abortion-rule-known-as-mexico-city-policy-11611835467"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Mr. Biden has reversed a rule }}}\uc2  known as the "Mexico City policy" that bars foreign nongovernmental groups that get U.S. funding from providing abortions or \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  information. Recent Democratic administrations have ended the policy, and Republican administrations {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/donald-trump-reinstates-antiabortion-policy-for-overseas-groups-1485194380"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 have reinstated it }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The administration has also moved to reverse a Trump-era rule that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-administration-curbs-federal-funding-for-clinics-providing-abortions-11550866834"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut off federal funding for family-planning organizations }}}\uc2  such as Planned Parenthood. And the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  has temporarily lifted a restriction on medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the pandemic and is now conducting a broader review of those policies.\par \par \uc2 While advocates on the left have praised those moves, they want stronger condemnation of state laws restricting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access and more robust support for bills such as the Equal Access to \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Coverage in Health Insurance Act, which would overturn Hyde, and the Women's Health Protection Act, which would limit states' abilities to implement \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. Both bills have been introduced in Congress in past years. The EACH Act has been reintroduced in this Congress and the Women's Health Protection Act is expected to be introduced in the coming weeks.\par \par \uc2 Gretchen Borchelt\uc2 , vice president for \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  and health at the \uc2 National Women's Law Center\uc2 , said the stakes were raised after the Supreme Court agreed to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 take the Mississippi case }}}\uc2 . She said Mr. Biden must be "clear and unequivocal in his support for people's right and ability to access \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 Several advocates complained that Mr. Biden didn't use the word \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a statement marking the anniversary of Roe v. Wade, the 1973 Supreme Court decision recognizing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, or in his recent address to a joint session of Congress.\par \par \uc2 White House press secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  said recently that the president was "committed to codifying Roe" into law regardless of the outcome of the Supreme Court case.\par \par \uc2 Mallory Quigley, a spokeswoman for \uc2 Susan B. Anthony\uc2  List, an antiabortion group, said Mr. Biden doesn't often highlight the issue, but she said that this was the "most pro \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  administration that has ever been."\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  Rights\par \par \uc2 More WSJ coverage on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions, selected by the editors\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-ban-11621452346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas Governor Signs Fetal-Heartbeat \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban }}}\uc2  (May 19)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Mississippi \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Case at the Supreme Court: What You Should Know }}}\uc2  (May 18)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-decide-if-kentucky-attorney-general-can-maintain-abortion-law-defense-11617035582"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court to Decide if Kentucky Attorney General Can Maintain \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Law Defense }}}\uc2  (March 29)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/arkansas-governor-signs-bill-that-bans-most-abortions-11615330493"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Arkansas Governor Signs Bill That Bans Most Abortions }}}\uc2  (March 9)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/south-carolina-passes-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-legislation-11613599308"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina Passes 'Fetal Heartbeat' \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Legislation }}}\uc2  (Feb. 17)\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bidens-budget-to-spotlight-battle-over-abortion-restrictions-11622118882"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden's Budget to Spotlight Battle Over \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Restrictions }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210527eh5r001p5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
