\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Texas Governor Signs Fetal-Heartbeat  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Ban; The Texas bill comes as the Supreme Court weighs the right to an  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jacob Gershman \par \uc2 497 \uc2 words\par \uc2 19 May 2021\par 19:25 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Texas's Republican Gov. Greg Abbott signed a bill on Wednesday that would ban most abortions after six to eight weeks, joining other Republican-led states in a push to outlaw the procedure as {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the right to an \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  is facing a Supreme Court review }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Texas statute, which is almost certain to face a legal challenge, makes it unlawful for a physician to terminate a fetus with a detectable heartbeat, which generally occurs six to eight weeks into a pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 The restriction makes an exception for medical emergencies. It doesn't impose criminal penalties, as do a number of other state abortions bans. Rather, it authorizes private citizens to bring civil enforcement actions against physicians and others for violations.\par \par \uc2 Doctors found liable would face damages of at least $10,000 for every \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  deemed unlawful. The person paying for the procedure could also be subject to liability.\par \par \uc2 The Republican-led state Senate and House passed the measure this month with votes almost entirely split along party lines. Between the two chambers, only two Democrats voted for the bill. No Republicans voted against the ban.\par \par \uc2 At the bill signing, Mr. Abbott said the legislation "ensures that the life of every unborn child who has a heartbeat will be saved from the ravages of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 The law set an effective date of Sept. 1.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups vowed to stop it. "The governor's swipe of a pen can't change the Constitution," the ACLU of Texas tweeted on Wednesday, calling the measure the most extreme \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  legislation enacted in Texas.\par \par \uc2 Around a dozen other states have enacted fetal-heartbeat \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. Courts have consistently found the measures to be unconstitutional and blocked states from enforcing them.\par \par \uc2 Conservative statehouses have escalated efforts to outlaw \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the constitutionally protected right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  is being revisited. The Supreme Court on Monday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-consider-abortion-restrictions-from-mississippi-11621259099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 said it would hear a challenge to a Mississippi law }}}\uc2  that bans abortions after about 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 Starting with the Roe v. Wade decision in 1973, the Supreme Court recognized a woman's constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 . That precedent and other rulings since have effectively barred states from restricting abortions before the point at which the fetus has reached the stage of viability\u8212\'20\'14at around 24 to 28 weeks into pregnancy\u8212\'20\'14when capable of surviving outside the womb.\par \par \uc2 In taking up the Mississippi case, the Supreme Court said it would re-examine the question of whether bans on pre-viability, elective abortions are unconstitutional. With conservatives now holding six of the court's nine seats, the case has the potential to rewrite a long-held precedent and make laws such as the statute Texas just enacted far less vulnerable to court challenge.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jacob Gershman at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jacob.gershman@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jacob.gershman@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/texas-governor-signs-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-ban-11621452346"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Texas Governor Signs Fetal-Heartbeat \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Ban  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210519eh5j004h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
