\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 The Mississippi  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Case at the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  : What You Should Know; The nation's highest court has agreed to revisit a core precedent stemming from its landmark Roe v. Wade\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jacob Gershman \par \uc2 810 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 May 2021\par 11:29 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The question of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights is making a return to the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  , with justices on Monday {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-consider-abortion-restrictions-from-mississippi-11621259099"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 agreeing to hear a challenge  }}}\uc2  to a Mississippi law that bans abortions after about 15 weeks of pregnancy.\par \par \uc2 More directly than in other recent \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  cases, the court is positioned to revisit the long-recognized constitutional right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before fetal viability that stems from its landmark 1973 Roe v. Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 Here are some questions and answers about the case and its implications.\par \par \uc2 What is the case the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  is reviewing?\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  said it would hear the case titled {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/search.aspx?filename=/docket/docketfiles/html/public/19-1392.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Organization  }}}\uc2 . At issue is a challenge to Mississippi's Gestational Age Act, a 2018 law that prohibited doctors from performing abortions after 15 weeks of gestation except in medical emergency or in case of severe fetal abnormality.\par \par \uc2 Jackson Women's Health Organization, the only licensed \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  facility in the state, sued to overturn the law. A district court and a federal appeals court said the law was unconstitutional, prompting Mississippi's appeal to the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  .\par \par \uc2 Jackson Women's Health {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/19/19-1392/150668/20200819155412230_39883 pdf Scott.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has said  }}}\uc2  the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  had no reason to take the case, pointing to "an unbroken line of decisions over the last fifty years" that it said cemented the unconstitutionality of banning \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  before the fetus attains viability. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/19/19-1392/145658/20200615170733513_FINAL Petition.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The state argued  }}}\uc2  that scientific understanding of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and its medical risks warrants a fresh look at prior holdings, saying its law advances the state's interest in protecting maternal health and avoiding fetal pain.\par \par \uc2 What specific question is the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  addressing?\par \par \uc2 When it agreed to review the case, the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  said it would address a single question: "whether all pre-viability prohibitions on elective abortions are unconstitutional."\par \par \uc2 What has the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  said about the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  pre-viability?\par \par \uc2 With its 1973 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/410/113"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Roe v. Wade decision  }}}\uc2 , the \uc2 Supreme Court\uc2  first recognized the right to \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as a fundamental liberty. Before Roe, states could decide whether to criminalize \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and many at the time of the ruling permitted \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  only when necessary to save or preserve the mother's life. The 7-2 ruling in Roe struck down those laws as unjustified intrusions into personal liberty and privacy under the 14th Amendment and its Due Process Clause.\par \par \uc2 Roe said states couldn't restrict abortions during a pregnancy's first trimester. In 1992, the high court reaffirmed the core of Roe in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/505/833"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Planned Parenthood v. Casey  }}}\uc2 . But now, the freedom to have an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  was no longer pegged to a specific gestational age but to a vaguer threshold of fetal "viability," which the court has estimated at around 24 to 28 weeks into pregnancy. Virtually any regulation of abortions performed before viability was unconstitutional. The court hasn't since wavered from that holding.\par \par \uc2 Have the justices given any indication of how they will rule?\par \par \uc2 The court's decision to hear the Dobbs case means that at least four justices wanted to revisit the viability rule. The court grew more conservative under President Donald Trump , and the conservative movement as a whole has long argued that the right to an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lacks any basis in the Constitution itself.\par \par \uc2 Still, even with conservatives occupying six of the court's nine seats, it is far from clear how the court will come down. Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  is on record opposing Roe v. Wade, describing it as "grievously wrong." Justice \uc2 Samuel Alito\uc2  has consistently voted to uphold \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions. Both antiabortion and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights advocates have expected Republican-appointed Justices \uc2 Neil Gorsuch\uc2  , \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2  and \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  to take a more skeptical view of Roe and its progeny than the court has to date. Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  is seen as more of a wild card.\par \par \uc2 During his confirmation process in 2018, Justice Kavanaugh told a Republican senator {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/kavanaugh-says-roe-v-wade-is-settled-law-gop-senator-says-1534880240"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 that he considered the Roe decision "settled law."  }}}\uc2  Justice \uc2 Anthony Kennedy\uc2  's successor was also among the four dissenting votes\u8212\'20\'14with Justices Thomas, Gorsuch and Alito\u8212\'20\'14in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-strikes-down-louisiana-abortion-law-11593440418"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the court's 5-4 decision  }}}\uc2  last June striking down a Louisiana law requiring that any doctor who provides abortions obtain admitting privileges to a local hospital.\par \par \uc2 Stating he was adhering to precedent, Chief Justice Roberts in the Louisiana case joined with four liberal justices, including the late Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  , whom Justice Barrett later replaced.\par \par \uc2 The other three justices on the current court\u8212\'20\'14\uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  , \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  and \uc2 Elena Kagan\uc2  , all appointed by Democratic presidents\u8212\'20\'14have taken a broad view of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jacob Gershman at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jacob.gershman@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jacob.gershman@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/the-mississippi-abortion-case-at-the-supreme-court-what-you-should-know-11621337351"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 The Mississippi \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Case at the Supreme Court: What You Should Know  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210518eh5i001gt\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal6