\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 U.S. Restores  \highlight22\uc2 Reproductive Rights \highlight\uc2  Report in Global Survey; State Department's annual human-rights report also provided a detailed accounting of abuses committed in China\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jessica Donati \par \uc2 498 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 March 2021\par 23:04 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The Biden administration is resuming the practice of evaluating women's \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2  in various countries as part of the State Department's annual survey of global human rights, reversing a decision by the Trump administration.\par \par \uc2 The State Department released its annual human-rights report on Tuesday. The report said an addendum to be added later this year will cover {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/human-rights-report-by-u-s-singles-out-russia-china-and-iran-1524259613"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 previously dropped topics }}}\uc2 , including maternal mortality, access to contraception and reproductive healthcare. Those topics were last reported upon in 2016.\par \par \uc2 "Women's rights, including sexual and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive rights\b0 \highlight\uc2 , are human rights," Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  told reporters on Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 President Biden took steps during his first days in office {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-to-reverse-abortion-rule-known-as-mexico-city-policy-11611835467"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 to reverse the Trump administration's cut }}}\uc2  to funding for women's sexual and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2 . These moves included revoking President Trump's expansion of the Mexico City policy, or "global gag rule," which prevents federal funds from going to foreign-aid groups that perform abortions.\par \par \uc2 In line with previous years, the report provided a detailed accounting of human-rights abuses committed in China, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/u-s-declares-chinas-treatment-of-uighur-muslims-to-be-genocide-11611081555"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 accusing Beijing of genocide }}}\uc2  against its mostly Muslim Uyghur ethnic minority population.\par \par \uc2 Biden Administration\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/president-biden-to-nominate-11-judicial-candidates-in-first-attempt-to-put-imprint-on-federal-judiciary-11617102668"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden Underscores Diversity With First Judicial Nominees }}}\par \par \uc2 Mr. Blinken said the report didn't intend to single out U.S. adversaries but to provide an impartial accounting of the state of human rights around the world.\par \par \uc2 "We will hear from some countries, as we do every year, that we have no right to criticize them because we have our own challenges," he said. "Well, we know we have work to do."\par \par \uc2 Mr. Blinken listed the need to address systemic racism as one of the rights issues the U.S. needs to address. The State Department is currently seeking to promote increased diversity in its workforce.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Blinken said that the trend lines on human rights were moving in the wrong direction, singling out numerous countries for violations documented in the report.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/saudi-crown-prince-approved-operation-to-kill-khashoggi-u-s-report-says-11614363492"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Those included Saudi Arabia }}}\uc2 , for "appalling actions" targeting dissidents abroad, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/myanmar-protesters-return-after-security-forces-kill-90-people-including-children-11616942696"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 and Myanmar }}}\uc2  for a military crackdown on protesters that killed at least 90 people over the weekend. Mr. Blinken also devoted time to describe the Syrian government's attacks on schools, markets and hospitals, and atrocities reported out of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/eritrea-withdraws-from-ethiopias-restive-tigray-region-11616789855"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Ethiopia's Tigray region }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In addition, the State Department report provided a catalog of alleged rights abuses by the Indian government to suppress the freedom of expression in Kashmir. The U.S. is seeking closer ties with India as a means to counter Chinese influence in Asia.\par \par \uc2 The report included details of a crackdown on local politicians and activists as well as restrictions on internet access. India and Pakistan agreed to a cease-fire along their disputed border last month.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jessica Donati at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jessica.donati@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jessica.donati@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-administration-to-restore-section-on-womens-rights-to-global-survey-11617128929"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 U.S. Restores \b  \highlight22Reproductive Rights\b0 \highlight22  Report in Global Survey }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210330eh3u004bl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
