\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court to Decide if Kentucky Attorney General Can Maintain  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2 -Law Defense; Republican \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2  seeks further appeals after two court rulings invalidated state curbs on second-trimester abortions\b0\par\par\uc2 By Brent Kendall \par \uc2 478 \uc2 words\par \uc2 29 March 2021\par 16:33 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The Supreme Court on Monday agreed to decide whether Kentucky's Republican attorney general can step in to defend a state \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law after another official dropped the state's legal defense following two losses in court.\par \par \uc2 The case won't give the justices a direct opportunity to weigh in on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, but their eventual decision could clarify how much latitude an attorney general enjoys to keep litigation alive amid changes in a state's political leadership.\par \par \uc2 The underlying dispute involves a 2018 Kentucky law that sought to ban the procedure used most commonly in second-trimester abortions, known as dilation and evacuation.\par \par \uc2 An \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  clinic and two doctors challenged the law, and a federal trial judge in 2019 ruled the law placed an undue burden on a woman's constitutional right to terminate a pregnancy before viability. A federal appeals court later agreed, in a 2-to-1 ruling issued last year.\par \par \uc2 When the litigation began, Republican \uc2 Matt Bevin\uc2  was governor of Kentucky and Democrat \uc2 Andy Beshear\uc2  was attorney general. Mr. Beshear later defeated Mr. Bevin in the 2019 gubernatorial election, while Republican \uc2 Daniel Cameron\uc2  won the state race for attorney general.\par \par \uc2 After last summer's appeals court ruling against the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  law, Mr. Beshear's administration decided against making a further legal bid to defend it. Mr. Cameron then sought the right to intervene in the case so that he could ask the appeals court to reconsider the case and, if necessary, to appeal to the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 The appeals court rejected that request, again on a 2-to-1 vote.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court said Monday it would consider Mr. Cameron's appeal of that rejection. The Kentucky attorney general argues he has the right and authority to keep the case alive. A group of 20 other states filed an amicus brief urging the high court to hear the appeal.\par \par \uc2 The American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  , representing the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights plaintiffs in the case, said Mr. Cameron waited too late to intervene in the case and was seeking to make new legal arguments that the state had already forfeited.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court will hear arguments in the case during its next term, which begins in October.\par \par \uc2 Conservatives now {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/conservative-dominated-supreme-court-fulfills-nixon-era-dream-1539077401"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 hold a 6-3 majority  }}}\uc2  on the court after former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  appointed {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/amy-coney-barrett-set-to-be-confirmed-as-supreme-court-justice-11603721947"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three justices  }}}\uc2 , including Justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  , whose background suggests she may be skeptical of the current scope of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights. She replaced Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  , a leading court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ruth-bader-ginsburg-dies-11600472623"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 supporter of \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  rights  }}}\uc2  who died last year.\par \par \uc2 Write to Brent Kendall at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:brent.kendall@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 brent.kendall@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-to-decide-if-kentucky-attorney-general-can-maintain-abortion-law-defense-11617035582"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court to Decide if Kentucky Attorney General Can Maintain \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22 -Law Defense  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210329eh3t002p9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
