\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 South Carolina Passes 'Fetal Heartbeat'  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Legislation; Governor has said he would sign bill, making it latest state to enact  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  restriction that may be headed to \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\b0\par\par\uc2 By Valerie Bauerlein \par \uc2 502 \uc2 words\par \uc2 17 February 2021\par 22:01 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 The South Carolina House of Representatives passed a bill Wednesday that would ban most abortions after six to eight weeks, making it the latest of a dozen states testing the limits of federal law.\par \par \uc2 The legislation, known as a "fetal heartbeat" bill because the heart of a fetus typically begins beating around six to eight weeks, passed the state Senate in January following a GOP pickup of seats in the November election. Republican Gov. \uc2 Henry McMaster\uc2  has said he would sign it as soon as possible, which could be Thursday, after a final procedural reading in the House.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates say they will challenge the bill in court for infringing a woman's constitutional right to terminate a pregnancy, established in the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision. Many players on both sides say they expect courts to block the bill, as they have similar measures in Alabama, Mississippi and Georgia. Advocates on both sides say they expect states to pass more \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions after the confirmation of Justice \uc2 Amy Coney Barrett\uc2  in October gave the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  in October gave the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/what-trump-pick-amy-coney-barrett-could-mean-for-future-of-the-supreme-court-11601155192"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a 6-3 conservative majority  }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 South Carolina is the first state to pass new \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  restrictions since {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/amy-coney-barrett-set-to-be-confirmed-as-supreme-court-justice-11603721947"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice Barrett was sworn in  }}}\uc2 , according to the \uc2 Guttmacher Institute\uc2  , a research group supportive of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights.\par \par \uc2 State Rep. Todd Rutherford, minority leader, led dozens of Democrats in walking out of the House chamber at the start of debate Wednesday. He called the bill "blatantly unconstitutional" and said the legislature should focus on other issues like Covid-19 vaccine distribution, rather than getting involved in a potentially long and costly court challenge.\par \par \uc2 Hours later, Republican House Speaker Jay Lucas sent House security out to compel Democrats to return to the chamber for the vote, which fell largely along party lines.\par \par \uc2 Republicans cheered GOP Rep. Melissa Lackey Oremus after she tearfully described her decision not to go through with an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  when she was 16. Unborn babies "don't deserve to die just because their mother made a bad choice one night," she said.\par \par \uc2 More state-level legislation has been proposed to restrict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past year than any time since 2011, said \uc2 Elizabeth Nash\uc2  , a policy expert at Guttmacher. She attributed that to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/republicans-hold-off-democratic-bid-to-flip-state-legislatures-11604584839"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Republican gains in state legislatures  }}}\uc2  in November and former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  's appointment of three conservative justices during his term.\par \par \uc2 The Supreme Court's last major ruling on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  came in June, before liberal Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  died and was replaced by Justice Barrett. In a 5-4 decision, the Court {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-strikes-down-louisiana-abortion-law-11593440418"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 struck down a Louisiana law  }}}\uc2  that required \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doctors to have admitting privileges at nearby hospitals, reaffirming a 2016 ruling that invalidated a similar Texas regulation.\par \par \uc2 Write to Valerie Bauerlein at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:valerie.bauerlein@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 valerie.bauerlein@wsj.com  }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/south-carolina-passes-fetal-heartbeat-abortion-legislation-11613599308"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 South Carolina Passes 'Fetal Heartbeat' \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Legislation  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210217eh2h00795\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 rst=wsjo AND (abortion OR "reproductive rights" OR "reproductive health") AND (atleast5(abortion) OR atleast3("reproductive rights"))\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\w